window.MirchiSearch=[{"title":"Business & leaders · How a station earns repeat advertising revenue","url":"/radio-mirchi/business#booking","text":"How a station earns repeat advertising revenue Agree the brief The buyer selects a city, time slot and outcome. Deliver and verify Production records broadcasts and checks any missed spots. Review and renew Sales and the buyer review delivery, response and the next booking."},{"title":"Business & leaders · Audience and buyer","url":"/radio-mirchi/business#audience","text":"Audience and buyer The listener receives the programme for free. The advertiser pays to reach listeners in a selected city and time slot. For a café, an offer code can link some store visits to an ad. The station can confirm delivery using broadcast logs."},{"title":"Business & leaders · Campaign fees and event income","url":"/radio-mirchi/business#commercial-uses","text":"Campaign fees and event income A café can buy a host-led tasting as well as airtime. The fee covers agreed work. Venue, staffing and production costs reduce the money the station keeps. A ticketed event can also earn admission and sponsor income according to the organiser’s agreement."},{"title":"Business & leaders · Client objectives and campaign delivery","url":"/radio-mirchi/business#client-examples","text":"Client objectives and campaign delivery A car, a home appliance, a tin of paint and an insurance policy are bought in different ways. That is why these four companies used Mirchi differently. ENIL, the company that operates Radio Mirchi, described the work in its report for April 2024 to March 2025. MG Hector took the radio host to the showroom. Think about buying a car. An ad can help you remember the name, but you will probably want to sit in the car and drive it. Mirchi hosts took part in showroom test drives and talked about the car’s features with participants. For the showroom manager, the next question is simple: how many people who tried the car came back to discuss buying one? Xiaomi took its products to people’s homes. Instead of waiting for families to visit an electronics store, its Smart Home League brought demonstrations and challenges to ten residential communities. Residents could see the products in use. Posts about the activity were displayed more than a million times, according to ENIL. That tells Xiaomi how widely the posts appeared. To learn what residents bought afterwards, it would also need sales records. Dulux made the paint shops the centre of the story. Dulux sells through dealers: shop owners who stock its paint. It ran a display contest involving 20 selected dealers across five cities. Mirchi hosts visited shops, and entries were featured on radio and online. The people Dulux wanted to involve first were the shop owners themselves. A shop could earn recognition for a good display, and Dulux could give its products a more prominent place in the store. ACKO met people at a run. Insurance is usually something people think about when they need a policy. ACKO also appeared in neighbourhood activities and a Neon Run across five cities. The run gave people an enjoyable occasion to encounter the brand. A runner attending, remembering ACKO and later buying a policy are three different outcomes. The report describes the event and leaves the sales outcome open. These are examples of work delivered. The report gives no fee or profit for each client. ENIL FY25 annual report, pages 15 and 16 One number in plain English. For July to September 2026, ENIL said radio generated 53% of its Indian revenue. Imagine all the money its Indian businesses earned in that quarter as ₹100. About ₹53 came from radio. The figure describes revenue before costs. S2"},{"title":"Business & leaders · How are ENIL, Mirchi and Gaana connected?","url":"/radio-mirchi/business#company","text":"How are ENIL, Mirchi and Gaana connected? ENIL is the company. Mirchi is its radio and entertainment brand. Gaana is its music streaming service. ENIL stands for Entertainment Network (India) Limited. It belongs to the wider Times Group and publishes its own financial results. Group revenue figures belong to ENIL and carry a reporting period. S6 S2 Who pays whom? Imagine a Delhi café buying an ad on a Mirchi morning show. The café pays to reach listeners. A Gaana subscriber pays to listen to music. Both activities sit within ENIL’s business, but they earn money in different ways. S7 S5 Where do Mirchi Plus and Mirchi Live fit? Mirchi Plus is a name readers may see on digital content and app listings. Mirchi Live is where people can find events and campaigns such as Mirchi Freshers. S20 S12"},{"title":"Business & leaders · ENIL leadership and group responsibilities","url":"/radio-mirchi/business#leaders","text":"ENIL leadership and group responsibilities View company leadership and responsibilities Leader Role in latest presentation Business responsibilities to clarify Yatish Mehrishi Chief Executive Officer Portfolio choices, profitable growth, capital discipline. Preeti Nihalani Chief Operating Officer City execution, pricing, sales enablement and cross-functional delivery. Sumit Aggrawal Chief Strategy & Growth Officer Growth opportunities, partnerships and scalable operating models. Udit Tyagi Chief Digital Officer Digital product, technology and experimentation. Sanjay Ballabh Chief Financial Officer Margins, collections, revenue and costs for each user group and investment trade-offs. Titles above follow the Q2 FY27 presentation; discussion themes are my analytical topics, not stated individual mandates. S1 S8"},{"title":"Business & leaders · What is difficult to reproduce","url":"/radio-mirchi/business#assets","text":"What is difficult to reproduce Analysis Local relevance A useful city personality understands language, humour, neighbourhoods and cultural timing. Treat that relationship as a product asset, with editorial judgment and talent continuity. Analysis Advertiser relationships A local sales relationship can open doors for several formats. The product challenge is making offers easy to understand, deliver and measure without fragmenting ownership. Analysis IP and execution A recognisable format can travel across cities, but execution depends on local demand, venue economics and sponsor fit. A repeatable playbook should preserve local relevance."},{"title":"Business & leaders · How central teams and city teams could work together","url":"/radio-mirchi/business#operations","text":"How central teams and city teams could work together Central: product platform, analytics definitions, rights standards, billing rules, experimentation and reusable creative tooling. City: programming, local creators, advertiser relationships, event partners and cultural adaptation. Shared governance: deal approval, sponsorship fulfilment, audience permissions and profit after direct costs reporting. Who can make each decision: ask which team manages the account, product budget, pricing, agreed delivery standard and how revenue is allocated across teams. This is a proposed working model for discovery. It does not claim to describe ENIL’s current reporting lines."},{"title":"Business & leaders · International: a local diaspora business","url":"/radio-mirchi/business#international","text":"International: a local diaspora business ENIL’s public profile describes a presence in the USA, UAE, Qatar and Bahrain. Its FY26 operating review discusses diaspora engagement and partnership / licensing opportunities. These are company disclosures, not a fresh station-by-station international audit. S7 S5 Commercial lever Question to investigate Diaspora relevance Which language, music and community formats create a repeat habit in each market? Local advertiser demand What customer categories pay for access, and how concentrated are the accounts? Operating structure Which markets are owned, operated with partners, franchised or licensed, and who bears the cost? Rights and distribution Which content can cross borders, and on which digital or broadcast platforms? Capital discipline What local profit after direct costs, cash commitment and partner performance justify expansion? International growth should be evaluated market by market. A recognisable Indian brand can help acquisition, but local demand, rights and execution still determine the economics."},{"title":"How Mirchi earns · Follow one radio booking","url":"/radio-mirchi/revenue#diagram-1","text":"Follow one radio booking 30 broadcasts A café orders a message that lasts 20 seconds. 600 ad seconds 30 broadcasts × 20 seconds each. ₹30,000 in revenue At an example price of ₹50 per second, before costs. Illustration only. Actual prices depend on the station, time and agreement."},{"title":"How Mirchi earns · How the money is made","url":"/radio-mirchi/revenue#streams","text":"How the money is made Engine Buyer / value purchased Revenue logic Costs and constraints Paid radio ad time Advertiser buys scheduled exposure to a city audience. Sold ad seconds × actual actual price earned. Finite inventory, discounts, agency terms, seasonality, programming and station costs. Integrated brand solutions Brand buys an idea executed across RJ content, on-ground and digital touchpoints. Project fee, sponsorship package or contracted deliverables. Production, talent, vendors, revisions and delivery complexity. Events & IP Sponsors, ticket buyers and commercial partners. Sponsorship + net ticket receipts + contracted ancillary income. Artists, venue, production, permits, security, marketing, refunds and cash advances. Digital solutions Advertiser buys content, creators, inventory or managed campaign work. Campaign/service fee; recognise revenue according to contract and accounting policy. Creator fees, paid media, production, platform dependence; billing that includes money passed on to partners can inflate gross revenue. Gaana Listener or distribution partner buys premium access. Subscription / partnership consideration over time covered by the plan. Rights, payment/channel fees, support, tech, acquisition and retention. International Local advertisers, partners and diaspora audiences. Market-specific operations, partnerships or licensing structures. Local regulation, rights, currency and partner economics. Business categories are grounded in ENIL disclosures; the formulas describe commercial mechanics and are analytical, not published ENIL rate cards. S7 S5"},{"title":"How Mirchi earns · The radio equation","url":"/radio-mirchi/revenue#radio-math","text":"The radio equation Model Net Revenue from paid radio ad time = ad seconds available × percentage of ad time sold × actual revenue per second. Use the same city, time of day and time period for every input. A 5% price reduction needs more than 5% additional sold volume to keep revenue unchanged: 1 ÷ 0.95 − 1 = 5.26%. If capacity or listener ad tolerance is already constrained, the extra volume may not be achievable. Discounting should be evaluated against total profit after direct costs, advertiser retention and future pricing expectations. Percentage of ad time sold and price are not independent. Prime time, local festivals, premium sponsorships and bundled contracts alter the inventory mix. A national average can hide both healthy cities and weak stations."},{"title":"How Mirchi earns · From advertiser brief to repeat budget","url":"/radio-mirchi/revenue#sales","text":"From advertiser brief to repeat budget Step Product / process opportunity Commercial measure Define objective One city, one audience, one business outcome, one budget range. Qualified brief to proposal rate. Package offer Standard modules with explicit deliverables and optional custom work. Proposal time and profit after delivery costs at quote. Approve & collect Margin review, advance collection and cancellation terms. Cash collected before committed vendor spend. Execute One delivery plan linking radio logs, creator assets and event tasks. On-time fulfilment and rework cost. Report & renew Show delivered media separately from response and causal lift. Repeat booking and profit from renewals. Recommended product principle: make the next purchase easier without promising giving credit for a result precision that the campaign design cannot support."},{"title":"How Mirchi earns · Questions that prevent misleading revenue stories","url":"/radio-mirchi/revenue#accounting","text":"Questions that prevent misleading revenue stories Is ticket revenue shown gross or net of platform fees, taxes and organiser share? Is an event owned, co-produced, commissioned or only promoted? Branding alone does not establish IP ownership. Do digital solutions include media purchased on behalf of clients? Separate billings from retained margin. When is sponsorship cash collected versus recorded as revenue? Does a bundle pay Gaana on shipment, activation or usage? What is the effective net consideration? Are sold to existing customers revenues extra or shifted from another Mirchi budget?"},{"title":"Radio & advertisers · What radio does well","url":"/radio-mirchi/radio#role","text":"What radio does well A useful radio proposition combines music with familiar personalities, local context, timely information and participation. The commercial product is access to that relationship. A listener who enjoys an RJ is not automatically a digital user or a ticket buyer; every handoff still has to earn the next action. The corporate profile lists 73 stations in 63 cities, with the listener figure on that page explicitly dated to IRS 2019. Use it to understand historical scale, not current unique reach. S7"},{"title":"Radio & advertisers · A senior PM’s radio dashboard","url":"/radio-mirchi/radio#inventory","text":"A senior PM’s radio dashboard Question Metric to inspect Decision Where is value leaking? City × station × time of day actual price earned, percentage of ad time sold and profit after direct costs. Price, bundle or inventory allocation. Which advertisers repeat? User group repeat spend, category, account size and collections. Strengthen the proposition for valuable segments. Are campaigns delivered? Booked versus aired spots, make-goods and exceptions. Fix delivery reliability before expanding promises. What does the audience tolerate? Ad minutes, tune-out signals where measurable, complaints and listener research. Protect experience while selling inventory. Does a cross-channel campaign work? Tagged response and an agreed extra results caused by the change design. Prove impact at the appropriate confidence level. These are metrics to request internally. No internal dashboard or listening panel was available for this study."},{"title":"Radio & advertisers · Proposed pilot: a local advertiser return loop","url":"/radio-mirchi/radio#pilot","text":"Proposed pilot: a local advertiser return loop Analysis Customer need A local business needs a credible way to bring relevant people to a store or offer, and an easy way to decide whether to buy another campaign. It may have neither a marketing analyst nor a full agency. Analysis Minimum product Create a scoped campaign brief, a verified landing page or call response mechanism, a delivery log and a concise close-out report. Sell a bounded test before automating the entire sales process. Analysis Validation Select a small, comparable advertiser user group; predefine one primary outcome. Use matched stores or time/geographic comparison groups that do not receive the change when practical. Report uncertainty, not just attributed clicks. Success criterion to agree before launch: higher extra profit after direct costs from repeat advertisers with acceptable collection days, no rise in delivery exceptions and no deterioration in listener experience."},{"title":"Radio & advertisers · Rights and regulatory dependencies","url":"/radio-mirchi/radio#constraints","text":"Rights and regulatory dependencies FM broadcast, online streaming, podcasts, social clips and event music can have different rights and contract conditions. Obtain a rights review for each intended reuse rather than treating a broadcast licence as permission for every platform. The government’s 2024 expansion announcement sets a 4% annual licence fee for the specified new-city channels. This must not be assumed to replace all existing ENIL licence obligations. S28 The station should establish how renewal exposure and regulatory changes enter deciding where to invest money. Treat potential reforms as scenarios, not approved future savings."},{"title":"Radio & advertisers · Know the frequency, but check the city","url":"/radio-mirchi/radio#frequencies","text":"Know the frequency, but check the city The September MIB list includes Mirchi at 98.3 MHz in Delhi, and at both 98.3 and 95 MHz in Bengaluru. Frequencies and brand variants vary by market; “98.3” is not the complete network map. S35 Before discussing a particular city, verify the current station, format, listener proposition and advertiser set. A second frequency should be evaluated on audience and commercial differentiation rather than assumed to be duplicate reach."},{"title":"Users & their needs · Who matters for each buying decision?","url":"/radio-mirchi/users#priority","text":"Who matters for each buying decision? Morning show. The commuter chooses the programme. A café buys repeated local ads. A booking code helps count responses, while the station log confirms delivery. This is an illustrative use case. Showroom campaign. The dealer pays, prospective drivers participate and the host introduces the product. Count completed drives, the dealer’s follow-up and the contribution from repeat bookings. College event. Students participate, a sponsor funds agreed activities and organisers manage entry. Check attendance, sponsor delivery and direct costs. Ticket receipts depend on the agreement. Documented client campaigns"},{"title":"Users & their needs · The customer map","url":"/radio-mirchi/users#needs","text":"The customer map Customer Job to be done What good looks like Research to run Local listener / commuter “Keep me company and connected to my city.” Relevant hosts, easy tuning, predictable experience. Diary study by commute / time of day, city and language. Music subscriber “Play something I want, quickly, without interruptions.” Relevant discovery, reliable playback and clear access. Task tests plus funnel and subscriber groups. Story / RJ fan “Let me follow this voice or series wherever I am.” Correct episode, continuity and meaningful release alerts. Follow one series from social discovery to repeat listening. Event attendee “Help me choose a worthwhile, smooth outing.” Clear price and rules, dependable entry and experience. Journey interviews including non-buyers and no-shows. Advertiser / agency “Reach the right people and justify the next budget.” Clear scope, dependable delivery and honest measurement. Win/loss interviews and repeat-spend analysis. Sponsor “Own an audience moment with credible value.” Contracted visibility, engagement and documented fulfilment. Sponsor review before and after each edition. RJ / creator / operations team “Help me make and deliver quality work efficiently.” Fast tools, rights clarity, fair control and fewer handoffs. Observe real production and campaign workflows. These are needs-based hypotheses, not claims from completed customer interviews."},{"title":"Users & their needs · Segment by behaviour before adding demographics","url":"/radio-mirchi/users#segmentation","text":"Segment by behaviour before adding demographics Audio: language, entry intent, content affinity, time of day, device, connection quality and paid status. Events: city, group size, format, first versus repeat attendance, purchase lead time and budget. Advertisers: objective, category, geography, budget, buying frequency, agency involvement and credit profile. Partnership user groups: redemption, listening activation, service duration, renewal eligibility and profit after direct costs. A single retention number can hide a strong existing subscriber base and a weak partner-acquired user group. Define the population and the moment the clock starts before comparing groups."},{"title":"Users & their needs · Discovery plan with evidence standards","url":"/radio-mirchi/users#research","text":"Discovery plan with evidence standards Analysis Qualitative Interview customers who completed the job and those who abandoned it. Observe the task rather than asking which feature they want. Recruit beyond vocal fans and recent complainants. Analysis Quantitative Validate event and account identity, payment outcomes and instrumentation before using funnels. Segment by channel and release version so a rollout does not look like a behavioural trend. Analysis Decision Write the evidence that would change the proposed priority. A hypothesis should be easy to reject when research shows the need is small, already met or too costly to serve."},{"title":"What I would improve · Measure local advertiser renewals","url":"/radio-mirchi/opportunities#advertiser","text":"Measure local advertiser renewals Offer a limited catalogue by objective, city and budget, supported by a clear delivery plan and response measurement. Start with a category that repeats frequently enough to evaluate within a practical window. A sales-assisted workflow is a reasonable first version; self-service comes after the offer is repeatable. Primary: extra 90-day advertiser profit after direct costs and repeat booking. Checks that protect service and profit: collection days, deal discount, delivery exceptions, sales time and listener experience. Evidence: matched accounts or a phased rollout; track displaced radio or solution spend. Stop: higher gross billings with lower retained margin or longer credit exposure."},{"title":"What I would improve · Evaluate repeat events","url":"/radio-mirchi/opportunities#events","text":"Evaluate repeat events Put event discovery, booking partners, sponsor fulfilment and the event budget into one operating view. Preserve attendee consent and ticket-platform contractual boundaries. The product should support a faster, better proceed or stop decision, not merely make another listing page. Primary: actual edition profit after direct costs and cash conversion. Customer: entry wait, issue resolution, sponsor fulfilment and subsequent return. Scale: comparable editions meet economics and service gates across cities. Stop: the model depends on uncontracted sponsorship, unrealistic attendance or unsustainable local workload."},{"title":"What I would improve · Improve content discovery and production","url":"/radio-mirchi/opportunities#ai","text":"Improve content discovery and production For content continuity, start with one franchise and preserve the destination from social post to story page to app. For AI, observe a real workflow first: transcription, clip selection, tagging, local adaptation or campaign report assembly may be candidates. Compare turnaround and error rate against the current process. Quality and rights are part of the product Keep editorial review, talent permission, licensed-use boundaries and factual checks in the release criteria. A faster output is valuable only if it is usable and creates no extra correction or rights burden."},{"title":"How to measure success · The main measures and what drives them","url":"/radio-mirchi/metrics#tree","text":"The main measures and what drives them Business Outcome Leading measures Checks that protect service and profit Radio Profit after direct costs from retained advertisers Actual price earned, percentage of ad time sold, repeat spend, delivery. Ad load, discount leakage, credit days, make-goods. Events Actual edition profit after direct costs and cash recovery Paid attendance, actual income per ticket after deductions, sponsor collections, repeat intent. Safety, entry wait, refunds, vendor exposure, fulfilment. Gaana Profit from subscribers who stay Intent-to-play, paid access success, retained listening days, renewal user groups. Playback reliability, support cost, refunds, partner economics. Digital solutions Profit kept after delivery costs per client Proposal speed, win rate, repeat scope, on-time delivery. Pass-through spend, rework, collections and concentration. Content Useful retained audience and attributable commercial value Repeat consumption, series completion, qualified handoffs. Rights, quality, creator workload and platform dependence. A proposed shared lens is extra profit after direct costs from repeat customer relationships . It needs a business-specific definition; a sponsor, an advertiser and a subscriber cannot share one base number."},{"title":"How to measure success · Definitions that need to be explicit","url":"/radio-mirchi/metrics#definitions","text":"Definitions that need to be explicit Activation: a successful value moment, not an install or a login. Define the required listening or campaign outcome before measurement. Retention: the fraction of a starting user group that meets the defined value event in a later window. Keep trial, partner and paid user groups separate. Profit after direct costs: net recorded revenue minus the costs included in the agreed cost breakdown. State which variable, direct and allocated costs are included. Extra results caused by the change: the change versus a credible estimate of what would have happened without the change, not the number of people with a campaign tag. Repeat event customer: one person attending a second relevant edition, counted once using information they have permitted us to link. Actual price earned: actual revenue after discounts and the adjustments agreed with finance."},{"title":"How to measure success · The important rates, with simple formulas","url":"/radio-mirchi/metrics#rate-formulas","text":"The important rates, with simple formulas Measure How to calculate it What to keep consistent First-play conversion People with a successful first play ÷ eligible people who entered the journey × 100. Use people, not a mixture of visits, installs and accounts. Define a successful play. 7-day / 30-day return People from the starting group who listen in the chosen later window ÷ people in that starting group × 100. State whether you mean exactly day 7, any day in week 2, or a rolling window. Episode completion Eligible episode starts that reach the agreed completion point ÷ eligible starts × 100. State the completion threshold; report episode length and repeated starts separately. Paid renewal Subscriptions that renew successfully ÷ subscriptions due to renew in the period × 100. Separate annual, monthly, trial and partner plans. A cancelled future renewal is not always immediate loss of access. Revenue per paying user Subscription revenue for a period ÷ the agreed average number of paying users in that period. State monthly or annual, exclude or include taxes consistently, and separate paying from active users. Customer acquisition cost Included marketing, partner and incentive spend ÷ new paying customers from that spend. A device shipped or a free trial started is not a paying customer. Radio ad-time sold Ad seconds sold ÷ ad seconds available for sale × 100. Compare the same city, station, time of day and period. Radio price earned Recorded ad revenue after agreed adjustments ÷ ad seconds sold. Use the same treatment of agency fees, discounts and bundles. Advertiser repeat rate Advertisers who buy again in the chosen window ÷ advertisers eligible to buy again × 100. Also measure repeat spend and profit: one small repeat order can hide lost budget. Booking conversion Completed paid bookings ÷ eligible booking journeys started × 100. Track people, orders and tickets separately; a couple ticket is not one attendee. Paid attendance Paid-ticket holders who enter ÷ valid paid-ticket holders expected × 100. Separate complimentary passes, refunds, no-shows and capacity. Sponsor renewal Eligible sponsors who book the next comparable edition ÷ eligible sponsors × 100. Also compare retained sponsorship value, cash collected and delivery costs. Event direct profit Sponsor income + ticket income after deductions + other contracted income − included event delivery costs. List the included costs. Direct profit is not the same as final company profit. AI usable-output rate AI outputs accepted after the agreed review ÷ outputs reviewed × 100. Include review time, correction time, rights checks and serious errors when judging value."},{"title":"How to measure success · Three experiments worth designing properly","url":"/radio-mirchi/metrics#experiments","text":"Three experiments worth designing properly Experiment Primary test Design caution Partner activation journey Extra profit from users who keep returning per eligible user group. Randomise or phase within comparable partner user groups; preserve offer and season. Advertiser package 90-day repeat profit after direct costs versus current offer. Account for sales selection, account size and spending shifted from an existing offer. Event reminder / return loop Extra net ticket profit after direct costs from permitted audience. Use a comparison group that does not receive the change; include discount cost, refunds and substitution between events. Choose sample size from the actual starting result, the smallest improvement worth detecting, allocation and desired statistical precision. No sample-size number is invented here. Predefine the decision window and checks that protect service and profit, and avoid repeatedly stopping the test at the first positive result."},{"title":"How to measure success · How to measure results across offline and online","url":"/radio-mirchi/metrics#attribution","text":"How to measure results across offline and online On-air codes, tagged links, unique landing pages, booking references and matching customer records can identify observed response. They do not automatically capture all radio exposure or establish causation. Pair response tracking with comparison groups that do not receive the change or matched comparisons where feasible, and report uncertainty. The stakeholder-friendly dashboard Show what was delivered, what people did, what changed versus the comparison and how much profit after direct costs remained. Keep these four layers separate so a reach metric does not quietly become a revenue claim."},{"title":"Try the numbers · Event edition: profit after direct costs and break-even","url":"/radio-mirchi/lab#events","text":"Event edition: profit after direct costs and break-even All amounts are in rupees, excluding GST. Ticket price is net organiser receipt; no fees or taxes are deducted again. Variable cost is per paid attendee. Sponsorship and ancillary income must be contracted; allocated corporate overhead is excluded. Paid ticket capacity Paid occupancy (%) Net receipt per ticket (₹) Sponsorship (₹) Net ancillary income (₹) Fixed direct costs (₹) Variable cost per attendee (₹) Reset event assumptions Formula: profit after direct costs = paid attendees × (net ticket receipt − variable cost) + sponsorship + ancillary − fixed costs. Break-even attendees = ceiling(max(0, fixed − sponsorship − ancillary) ÷ ticket profit after direct costs), subject to positive ticket profit after direct costs and capacity."},{"title":"Try the numbers · Subscriber group: first-year profit after direct costs","url":"/radio-mirchi/lab#subscribers","text":"Subscriber group: first-year profit after direct costs This model starts with paying users. It is not suitable for treating a complimentary hardware bundle as full-price revenue. Annual price below is net recorded service revenue per paid year, excluding taxes. Cost-share and retention inputs are hypothetical, not Gaana disclosures. Starting paid users Annual net service revenue (₹) One-year paid renewal (%) Variable revenue-linked costs (%) Annual service cost per user (₹) Cost of getting a new customer per starting user (₹) Reset subscriber assumptions Formula: annual unit profit after direct costs before acquisition = annual net revenue × (1 − variable cost share) − annual service cost. First-year user group profit after direct costs subtracts acquisition spend. Renewal illustration applies the same revenue and costs for each customer to renewing users, excludes new acquisition and is not lifetime value."},{"title":"Try the numbers · Radio: percentage of ad time sold versus price","url":"/radio-mirchi/lab#inventory","text":"Radio: percentage of ad time sold versus price An illustrative period with a fixed pool of available ad seconds. Changing utilisation and price earned does not account for changes in station, time of day, inventory quality, collections or extra operating costs. Available ad seconds Percentage of ad time sold (%) Net revenue per second (₹) Alternative percentage of ad time sold (%) Alternative price discount (%) Reset radio assumptions Decision rule A revenue increase does not establish a profit increase. Use these models to expose assumptions, then add the actual cost, cash and customer constraints before recommending a decision."},{"title":"Market & competitors · Benchmark: one Delhi dealer seeking weekend test drives","url":"/radio-mirchi/competition#dealer","text":" For the change in listener behaviour, start with the India survey, the dated price comparison and the distinction between reported usage and inferred switching.  See the four-service comparison   Compare what a buyer can establish before asking for a quote. Each operator receives the same brief: a city show, a host appearance, digital follow-up and a record of delivery.    Mirchi.  Its MG Hector work demonstrates host-led showroom execution. Ask for Delhi schedules, replacement terms and a sample broadcast log.  ENIL FY25 annual report, pp. 15–16    Radio City.  Its Bazaar campaign provides a precedent for promoting local businesses. Ask whether a Delhi showroom visit and response tracking are available today.  Radio City Bazaar    RED FM.  Its Delhi page provides a dedicated advertiser contact. This reduces the work of finding the sales team. Request the host, time slot and delivery evidence in writing.  Delhi advertiser contact    BIG FM.  Public host, podcast and video listings give the dealer digital formats to discuss. Ask which Delhi slots, usage rights and host visits are inc"},{"title":"Market & competitors · The market is moving at different speeds","url":"/radio-mirchi/competition#market","text":" FICCI-EY estimates India’s 2025 M&E market at ₹2.78 trillion. Its March 2026 release reports radio down 7% to ₹23 billion, live events up 44%, and digital advertising up 26%. These are calendar-year industry estimates; they are not Mirchi growth rates.   S9    Inference: diversification is commercially sensible, but an attractive category does not make every entrant or format profitable. Mirchi should choose businesses where its relationships, IP and city execution create an advantage after extra cost. "},{"title":"Market & competitors · Competition by customer decision","url":"/radio-mirchi/competition#landscape","text":"     Arena  Relevant alternatives  What they compete on  Mirchi question      Local advertising  Radio City, RED FM, BIG FM, Fever, regional stations, local publishers, outdoor and digital ads.   S29   S30    Local reach, price, targeting, creative, delivery and evidence.  Why should a local advertiser renew this package?    Audio habit  Spotify, YouTube / YouTube Music, JioSaavn, Apple Music, Amazon Music and other audio services.  Catalogue, discovery, devices, reliability, price and convenience.  Which listening job can Gaana serve especially well?    Creator attention  YouTube, Instagram and independent regional creators.  Creator affinity, entertainment, distribution and community.  Can the creator relationship lead to an owned, useful service?    Going out  Concert promoters, local organisers, BookMyShow and District discovery.   S26   S27    Relevant supply, trust, availability, convenience and price.  Where does Mirchi add distinctive IP or execution value?    Brand solutions  Agencies, creator networks and platforms.  Strategy, creative quality, speed, measurement and commer"},{"title":"Market & competitors · What others offer, and what Mirchi offers in return","url":"/radio-mirchi/competition#comparison","text":"     Competitor  What they offer that Mirchi could learn from  What Mirchi or Gaana brings  What to test      Radio City and BIG FM  Both compete for local attention. BIG FM puts RJs, podcasts and videos in the main navigation.   S29   S30    Mirchi can connect regional stories, local sales teams, Gaana and physical events.   S1   S14    Test whether a city and RJ directory helps people find their intended host or show faster than the editorial landing page.    RED FM and Fever  Alternative local stations in several Mirchi markets. Check programming and ad packages city by city.   S35    Mirchi can offer advertisers campaigns across scheduled radio ads, creators, events and digital services.   S7    Compare actual prices, audiences, delivery and renewal for the same brief in the same city.    Spotify India  Dedicated student plan and a Platinum tier with lossless audio. No equivalent Gaana plan was confirmed on the public price page reviewed.   S37   S23    Gaana showed cheaper standard web pricing in this snapshot, a one-time annual option, and Mirchi originals such as Sunday Suspen"},{"title":"Market & competitors · Revenue, audience and engagement numbers","url":"/radio-mirchi/competition#numbers","text":"     Measure  Mirchi / Gaana  Benchmark  How to read it      Quarterly operating revenue  ENIL group ₹116.70 crore, down 17.3%.   S1    Music Broadcast ₹40.96 crore, up 8.2%, standalone.   S36    Same quarter ending September 2026. Scope and revenue mix differ, so this compares company direction and scale only.    Music audience  ENIL deck reports 20M Gaana monthly active users.   S1    Spotify reports 788M monthly active users and 306M Premium subscribers worldwide.   S38    Global Spotify is a scale reference. Gaana monthly users cannot reveal how many pay.    Listening activity  ENIL reports 30+ minutes per listening user in early Vivo engagement.   S1    No matching partner, population and time window verified.  Compare time per listening day, successful plays and repeat listening over 7 and 30 days within the same group.    India web price  Gaana ₹129 monthly, ₹709 yearly offer, ₹899 one-time annual.   S23    Spotify Standard ₹139 per month or ₹1,390 for one year. Student ₹69 per month.   S37    Public price snapshot. Check current offer and eligibility. These figures do not sho"},{"title":"Market & competitors · Which gaps I would investigate first","url":"/radio-mirchi/competition#next-moves","text":"  Start with three real tasks: find a favourite RJ or show, play a regional episode from a social link, and book a local event. Compare steps and completion on desktop, phone browsers and installed apps.  Compare radio advertisers in the same city, category and time of day. Track actual price per ad second, percentage of ad time sold, repeat booking and profit after delivery costs.  Compare streaming groups by how they joined. Track first play, return after 7 and 30 days, paid renewal, refunds and profit per customer.  Compare repeat event formats by city, capacity and sponsor structure. Track booking completion, paid attendance, refunds, sponsor renewal and cash received before committing to costs.   A public feature gap is a reason to test a customer task. Missing public numbers are listed as questions for the operating team and do not count against either company. "},{"title":"Market & competitors · A defensible position to test","url":"/radio-mirchi/competition#position","text":"   Analysis  Win locally  Connect an advertiser’s city objective with a credible host, useful local content and a relevant experience. Make delivery and response visible.    Analysis  Win through culture  Use regional voices and recognisable franchises to create a reason to return. Avoid a feature race with every large audio platform.    Analysis  Win through execution  A consistent operational experience can make a format easier for sponsors and attendees to repeat. Build repeatability around margin and service quality.   "},{"title":"Market & competitors · SWOT, tied to decisions","url":"/radio-mirchi/competition#swot","text":"     Lens  Assessment  Decision implication      Strengths  Brand, cultural relevance, local talent, advertiser relationships, content and execution capabilities.  Build around existing advantages rather than unrelated software products.    Weaknesses to investigate  Cross-platform continuity, variable economics by business, execution complexity.  Measure before calling them proven failures.    Opportunities  Better conversion of existing reach, retained paid user groups, repeat sponsor formats.  Pilot focused improvements with profit after direct costs as the success measure.    Threats  Ad-budget shifts, creator/platform dependence, rights costs, event competition and demand volatility.  Use scenario planning, diversified channels and explicit downside limits.     "},{"title":"Campaign prototype · How long does it take to recover the cost of a new subscriber?","url":"/radio-mirchi/prototype#digital","text":" Suppose a city show costs ₹30,000 to promote. Each active paying listener contributes ₹25 per month after variable costs. Choose a result to see how customer acquisition changes the decision. These are illustrative inputs.   150 extra payers  ₹30,000 ÷ 150 = ₹200 per payer. Recovering this takes eight paid months. If the typical payer leaves after four months, the campaign falls short by ₹100 per payer.    300 extra payers  ₹100 per payer takes four paid months to recover. A listener who leaves after two paid months contributes ₹50. Check the actual renewal distribution before expanding.    600 extra payers  ₹50 per payer takes two paid months. Check that the additional payers were caused by the campaign and that discounts did not reduce the ₹25 monthly contribution.    Change the assumptions in the financial calculator  "},{"title":"Campaign prototype · What the dealer bought","url":"/radio-mirchi/prototype#delivery","text":"  Objective:  encourage weekend test drives. The example booking covers 30 radio ads and one host appearance. The station log confirms 28 ads and the appearance. Two ads remain due. Agree replacement slots with the dealer. "},{"title":"Campaign prototype · What the dealer can measure","url":"/radio-mirchi/prototype#response","text":" The dealer recorded 18 test drives during the campaign weekend. Eight participants used the campaign booking code. Code use shows a recorded response. A comparable weekend or a controlled test would help estimate additional visits caused by the campaign. "},{"title":"Campaign prototype · Compare a renewal offer","url":"/radio-mirchi/prototype#offer","text":" Choose the proposed terms    Standard renewal  Discount and extra host time     All amounts and counts here are examples. The dealer sees delivery and response. The station uses the renewal calculation internally.  Read the pilot design "},{"title":"Campaign prototype · Listener product decision","url":"/radio-mirchi/prototype#listener","text":" Proposed pilot for one local show. Choose the observed result to see the next product decision. These are hypothetical outcomes.   People open the host’s link but rarely start listening  Check that the link opens the promised episode, the play control works on mobile web and the audio is available in that region. Compare successful plays per eligible visit before buying more traffic.    People listen once but seldom return  Test a visible next episode or a voluntary show reminder. Compare seven-day return among first-time listeners with the current experience, and monitor opt-outs.    Listeners return and a sponsor wants more ad time  Test one placement. Compare net sponsor income per eligible listener, completion and repeat listening against the current ad load. Expand only if the extra income covers production and the loss of future listening.  "},{"title":"Business case · Who needs a better product?","url":"/radio-mirchi#problem","text":"   The listener  A city commuter knows the host’s voice but may not know the show title. A short link should open the episode the host just mentioned.    The subscriber  A listener arriving through earbuds or a trial needs a reason to return after the offer ends. A saved local show can give them one.    The advertiser  A local buyer wants to know whether people listened, enquired or visited. Each outcome needs its own count and cost.    ENIL reported 153.1 million monthly active users across its digital properties and around 20 million for Gaana. These have different scopes and potentially overlapping audiences. Dividing one by the other would give a misleading conversion rate.  ENIL earnings call, November 2026  "},{"title":"Business case · Why start with returning listeners?","url":"/radio-mirchi#readout","text":" Gaana moved to paid streaming in 2022 while rivals could still introduce people to music for free. In YouGov’s urban India survey, Gaana usage fell from 32% to 22% between 2021 and 2024, while Spotify rose from 24% to 42%. A familiar city host is one reason to choose Mirchi that a competing music catalogue cannot reproduce.  See the four-service comparison    Which alternatives were considered?  A cheaper weekly pass may attract buyers who would have bought the monthly plan. Buying installs can increase acquisition cost. A local series can use existing distribution, but still costs money to produce and promote. Test repeat use first, then test a paid offer with listeners who have experienced the show.  "},{"title":"Business case · The proposed listening journey","url":"/radio-mirchi#solution","text":"   Discover  Hear a short address on FM or tap a tagged link on a social clip.    Listen  Open the exact episode in the app or a lightweight web player. Offer city and language selection only when useful.    Return  Save the show and resume it. Ask permission for a reminder when the next episode arrives.    Choose a plan  Explain the price, billing period and renewal before purchase. Offer a relevant series or a longer ad-free session.    The parallel advertiser opportunity is to sell sponsorship for a defined audience with evidence of delivery. Obtain rights and confirm eligible placements before quoting.  What M-Ping, Brewery and event sponsorship sell  "},{"title":"Business case · How to run a controlled pilot","url":"/radio-mirchi#pilot","text":" Weeks 1–2: the station producer selects a rights-cleared show. The digital team tests links on mobile web and installed apps. Analytics defines an eligible visitor and records playback, return and payment. Weeks 3–6: compare a direct episode landing page with the usual destination, using random assignment within each tagged source. Keep the same creative, programme and offer. Report FM and social separately. Weeks 7–10: follow each group for 30 days. Compare like-for-like listeners before extending the trial.   How much can the team spend?  Illustration: ₹30,000 in production and promotion divided by 300 additional paying listeners is ₹100 per new payer. At ₹25 a month left after variable costs per active payer, that takes four paid months to recover before churn. If many listeners cancel in month two, the campaign can lose money even with strong sign-ups.  Explore the payback scenarios   "},{"title":"Business case · When should Mirchi expand?","url":"/radio-mirchi#decision","text":" Primary decision: expand only if the test produces more returning listeners and positive additional contribution over the agreed payback window. Track first plays per eligible arrival, seven-day return per first-time listener, first paid renewal per eligible subscriber and contribution after rights, production, partner fees and promotion. Set the minimum useful lift and sample size with finance and analytics before launch.  Pause if playback failures, refund requests or complaints rise beyond the pre-agreed limits. A positive conversion result with weaker renewal calls for a longer observation window. If the listener trial succeeds, take a separately costed sponsorship package to a city advertiser.  Explore an advertiser campaign review  "},{"title":"Business case · Research appendix","url":"/radio-mirchi#map","text":"   Understand  Business & leaders  Follow one morning show from the listener’s seat to the advertiser’s desk, then see how Mirchi worked with four real businesses.    Understand  How Mirchi earns  Follow each source of income: radio ads, brand campaigns, events, digital services and Gaana subscriptions.    Understand  Financial results  The group reports these figures. Use the specifically labelled radio figures when discussing the radio business.    Businesses  Radio & advertisers  Understand paid ad time, pricing, local audiences and how to help advertisers get more value.    Businesses  Events & formats  The main event formats, how their income and costs work, and how to make people and sponsors return.    Businesses  Gaana & digital  Gaana is an ENIL business. For Radio Mirchi, the relevant question is how listeners find and return to its shows when content travels across services.    Understand  Users & their needs  A simple map of listeners, subscribers, event attendees, advertisers and sponsors, plus the questions I would test.    Understand  Market & competitors  Compare the "},{"title":"Financial results · How much of ENIL’s domestic revenue came from digital?","url":"/radio-mirchi/financials#digital-mix","text":" Compare the same July–September quarter each year. The figures below are the shares shown in ENIL’s Q2 FY27 investor presentation. The latest quarter includes Gaana and digital solutions. The 2023 acquisition changes the comparison across years.     Quarter  Digital share of domestic revenue      Q2 FY24     3.2%    Q2 FY25     11.5%    Q2 FY26     23.3%    Q2 FY27     29%     In Q2 FY27 digital earned ₹33 crore. On the earnings call, the CEO estimated Gaana at about ₹22 crore. The roughly ₹11 crore difference includes other digital activities. Management identified digital solutions as another large business without assigning it the entire remainder. A rising share can reflect both digital growth and weakness elsewhere. Digital revenue grew 4.6% year on year, while the digital operating loss narrowed to ₹7.5 crore.  Quarterly earnings discussion    ENIL Q2 FY27 presentation    Read the annual and quarterly numbers on their original basis  In its FY26 presentation ENIL compared digital platform revenue of ₹112.39 crore with ₹61.08 crore for FY25, an increase of 84%. Its earlier FY25"},{"title":"Financial results · What happened to Indian radio advertising?","url":"/radio-mirchi/financials#radio-results","text":" In July–September 2026, selling radio ad time generated less revenue. Management reported a 12.6% decline in commercial airtime revenue. Radio contributed 53% of domestic revenue. Applying this rounded share to ₹113.65 crore gives approximately ₹60 crore for radio. This is an estimate. The 16.1% decline in total domestic sales covers several businesses.  Earnings call  "},{"title":"Financial results · What these numbers mean","url":"/radio-mirchi/financials#plain-financials","text":"     Measure  Read it as      Revenue  Sales before costs.    EBITDA  Profit before interest, tax and the accounting charges that spread asset costs over years. It is not final profit or cash flow.    PAT  Profit after tax: the final profit or loss.    Domestic / consolidated  The domestic scope shown by ENIL / the group including subsidiaries. Do not mix their numbers.    Q2 FY27 / YoY  July to September 2026 / compared with the same quarter last year.    ₹ crore  ₹1 crore = ₹10 million.      Example: a company can sell more but make less profit if its costs grow faster. It can also improve EBITDA and still report a final loss. "},{"title":"Financial results · Latest quarter: Q2 FY27","url":"/radio-mirchi/financials#quarter","text":" Period: 1 July-30 September 2026. Released 3 November 2026. ₹ crore; ₹10 million = ₹1 crore. Figures below are presentation-defined operating income/revenue and EBITDA.   S1        Metric  Q2 FY27  Q2 FY26  YoY      Consolidated operating revenue  116.70  141.14  −17.3%    Consolidated EBITDA  12.05  11.38  +5.9%    Consolidated PAT  −4.86  −4.08  Loss widened    Domestic operating revenue  113.65  135.42  −16.1%    Domestic EBITDA  11.26  10.28  +9.5%       Do not mix the headlines  ₹11.3 crore / +9.5% is the rounded domestic EBITDA headline. ₹12.05 crore / +5.9% is consolidated EBITDA in the deck. Pair each profit number with the matching revenue scope.   S1   S2    "},{"title":"Financial results · Full-year and half-year context","url":"/radio-mirchi/financials#year","text":"     Scope / period  Operating revenue  EBITDA  PAT      Consolidated FY26  565.17  44.96  −7.39    Consolidated FY25  544.15  78.56  11.95    Consolidated H1 FY27  230.39  21.08  −10.86    Consolidated H1 FY26  258.08  18.95  −9.36      FY26 from the Q4 deck; H1 from the Q2 deck. FY26 EBITDA declined despite revenue growth; H1 FY27 EBITDA improved while revenue declined. Annual results and a six-month period are not directly comparable.   S4   S1    Calculated consolidated EBITDA margin: Q2 FY27  10.33%  versus  8.06%  a year earlier; FY26  7.96%  versus FY25  14.44% . These are ratios of the displayed operating figures. EBITDA is not cash flow or PAT. "},{"title":"Financial results · What the portfolio mix says","url":"/radio-mirchi/financials#mix","text":" Management reported approximately 53% radio and 29% digital in domestic Q2 revenue; the remaining approximately 18% covers events and other business. Digital revenue was about ₹33 crore and digital EBITDA loss about ₹7.5 crore. This is a rounded management mix, not a statutory segment reconciliation.   S2     Radio 53%  Digital 29%  Other 18%   Digital’s share can increase when radio declines. A higher percentage alone does not establish strong absolute digital growth. Evaluate growth, loss reduction and the quality of the acquired user groups together. "},{"title":"Financial results · Cash and operating costs","url":"/radio-mirchi/financials#cash","text":" September consolidated cash was reported at ₹371.5 crore. For March, the Q4 deck distinguishes consolidated cash of about ₹423.9 crore from standalone cash of ₹404.2 crore. Avoid presenting them as two estimates of the same scope.   S2   S4      Operating leverage:  station and platform costs do not fall instantly with ad demand. Efficiency can improve EBITDA before revenue recovers.   Below EBITDA:  depreciation/amortisation, finance costs, other income, exceptional items and tax can move PAT differently.   Event working capital:  vendor advances create cash exposure before ticket and sponsor collections.   Do not infer runway:  cash balances are not an unrestricted product budget; commitments, lease liabilities and investment plans matter.    Business interpretation  “I see improving operating discipline, but I would not declare the transformation complete. I would track profit after direct costs and cash by business and user group, while protecting the radio engine and proving repeatable economics in digital and events.”  "},{"title":"Financial results · How sales and profit changed year by year","url":"/radio-mirchi/financials#annual-trend","text":"     Financial year  Group operating income (₹ crore)  Growth over last year  Operating earnings before interest, tax and depreciation (₹ crore)  Profit after tax (₹ crore)      FY24, restated  538.43  See note below  105.87  32.98    FY25  544.15  +1.1%  78.56  11.95    FY26  565.17  +3.9%  44.96  −7.39      Sales rose for two years while operating earnings fell. By FY26, ENIL recorded a loss after tax. FY24 originally reported about ₹500 crore of group revenue, up 13.6% on its then-reported comparison. ENIL later revised the FY24 figures to include the acquired business. Use ₹538.43 crore when comparing FY25 with FY24. The FY27 half-year and quarter appear separately above.   FY25 presentation, restated consolidated comparison  ·  Original FY24 release    S4   S1   "},{"title":"Events & formats · Which Mirchi events can someone book or verify?","url":"/radio-mirchi/events#dated-events","text":" An active ticket page, a completed sponsor campaign and a concert mentioned by a journalist are different types of evidence. Here is what a buyer or attendee could verify on 23 November 2026.   Listed for sale · Mirchi Neon Run, Chennai  District listed the run at SPR City–Binny for Saturday 28 November 2026 at 6:00 PM, with tickets from ₹299. That shows a public offer to attendees. Ticket price alone cannot give Mirchi’s earnings after discounts, ticketing fees, taxes and production.  Dated ticket listing     Delivered · OPPO Mirchi Freshers Season 13  OPPO Reno16 was presenting sponsor and Croma associate sponsor. Students registered for a QR pass, interacted with the phone camera on campus and voted online. ENIL reported 50,000+ registrations, 90,000+ on-ground interactions and 5,000+ Pop Cam activations across a programme spanning 100 colleges and 16 cities. One person can interact several times. The campaign page persists, while the terms give a tentative end date of 30 September 2026.  Season terms  ·  ENIL Q2 FY27 presentation     Delivered · music, festivals and city busines"},{"title":"Events & formats · Know the portfolio and its status","url":"/radio-mirchi/events#portfolio","text":"     Property / format  Evidence / status  Business lesson      Mirchi Rock & Dhol  2026 Navratri listings across cities; now historical.   S11    Cultural demand can support repeated city editions; pricing and costs remain local.    Mirchi Neon Run  District lists Chennai, 28 Nov 2026, 6 PM, from ₹299. Upcoming listing at research date.   S26    Running plus entertainment can serve consumers and sponsors; verify the listing before attending.    Mirchi Freshers S13  Campaign website and terms: 100 colleges, 16 cities, Aug-Sep 2026 period.   S12   S13    A campus programme can join physical participation with a digital voting loop.    Mirchi Music Awards  Established IP; linked 16th-edition results are dated Dec 2024.   S15    Recognisable content can generate sponsor and distribution value; no unverified 2026 edition claimed.    SBI Green Marathon / Mindspace Eco Run  Reported in Q4 FY26 presentation.   S4    Commissioned or partner-led programmes can be commercially distinct from owned ticketed concerts.    Mirchi Holicious  BookMyShow 2026 listing marked event closed.   S27    Tick"},{"title":"Events & formats · The event income and cost sheet","url":"/radio-mirchi/events#economics","text":"     Revenue / cost line  What to verify      Sponsorship  Signed consideration, barter versus cash, deliverables, collections, cancellation clauses.    Ticketing  Paid admissions, average actual price earned, discounts, complimentary entries, refunds, platform fees and taxes.    Ancillary  Only contracted organiser share of stalls, hospitality or merchandise.    Direct cost  Artist, venue, stage, sound, production, permissions, security, medical, insurance and staffing.    Marketing & selling  Paid media, commissions, creative and attributable sales cost.    Downside  Weather, cancellation, artist non-appearance, demand shortfall and vendor commitments.    Cash & overhead  Timing of advances and settlements; show profit after direct costs separately from allocated corporate overhead.      The live calculator uses a simplified pre-tax profit after direct costs model. It is an illustration, not Mirchi’s actual event cost structure.  Open event economics lab . "},{"title":"Events & formats · The attendee journey is the retention product","url":"/radio-mirchi/events#journey","text":"   Discover:  relevant city, format, date, artist and accessible information; explain why this event fits the person.   Decide:  show total price, inclusions, age/access rules, transport information and cancellation terms before checkout.   Attend:  ticket retrieval, entry throughput, clear help, safe capacity, water and medical support.   Remember:  useful post-event content and feedback; obtain permission for future contact.   Return:  recommend the next relevant event, not every event nationwide. Reward repeat attendance only when extra margin pays for the benefit.  "},{"title":"Events & formats · Proposed event growth system","url":"/radio-mirchi/events#scale","text":" Start with one repeatable format in two contrasting cities. Give every edition a signed sponsor plan, a downside budget, a cash exposure ceiling and an attendee service plan. Link the promotion source to a first-party or partner-compliant event record so the team can understand conversion without double-counting.    Analysis  Before go / no-go  Secure minimum sponsorship and venue options. Track break-even paid admissions against realistic demand, then set spend-release gates.    Analysis  During execution  Use one operating checklist with named owners. Escalate queues, safety, artist delays and fulfilment gaps quickly. Capture only the data necessary for the intended service.    Analysis  After the edition  Close collections, vendor settlements and sponsor fulfilment. Compare actual profit after direct costs with the quote and track sponsor / attendee return over subsequent editions.   "},{"title":"Gaana & digital · Where does a Mirchi reader go, and who pays?","url":"/radio-mirchi/digital#live-products","text":"  Product check · 23 November 2026.  Mirchi Plus became part of Gaana. ENIL explicitly confirmed the integration in its FY24 annual report. Today a reader can start on Mirchi’s entertainment site and follow a show or subscription link to Gaana.  ENIL FY24 annual report  ·  Mirchi Stories     Read on Mirchi  Find a song chart, interview or photo story. The page carries labelled advertising space.    Choose a show  Trending Podcasts links to Gaana. Examples include Sunday Suspense, RJ Kartik Motivation and Mirchi Murga with RJ Naved.    Consider paying  The header offers a ₹1 introductory trial and a Gaana Plus purchase link. Eligibility, renewal price and billing terms depend on checkout.     How much does each activity earn?  ENIL disclosed ₹33 crore of digital revenue in July–September 2026. Its CEO estimated Gaana at about ₹22 crore. That leaves roughly ₹11 crore for the rest of digital. Management names digital solutions as the other large business and also refers to smaller components. Individual shows, ad formats, events and partners have no published revenue split here.  Earnin"},{"title":"Gaana & digital · What does each platform do for a listener?","url":"/radio-mirchi/digital#mirchi-plus","text":"  Mirchi creates the shows. ENIL integrated Mirchi Plus into Gaana, where readers can find featured podcasts and subscription offers.  ENIL operates the businesses. A Mirchi team can commission a series and promote it on air. Placement, entitlement and billing on Gaana require agreement with its product team.   Mirchi Plus on phones, the web and in cars  Launched in India in July 2022 with mobile web, Android and iOS. Launch coverage described short videos, original audio stories and podcasts in English, Hindi, Punjabi, Marathi, Gujarati, Bangla, Telugu, Tamil, Malayalam and Kannada. Its help centre lists Android Auto and Apple CarPlay. In the car, the useful task is starting or resuming audio hands-free. Video discovery belongs on a phone. Current device, regional catalogue and sign-in behaviour need an installed-device check.  Mirchi Plus help centre  ·  ENIL launch presentation  ·  Launch language list     Three journeys to test  A commuter hears a host mention a series and wants the exact episode. A social viewer taps a clip on mobile web and wants to listen before installing. A "},{"title":"Gaana & digital · How Gaana went from early leader to challenger","url":"/radio-mirchi/digital#gaana-history","text":"   2011 · Listening on the web  Gaana let people choose songs online. Its first month attracted about 1.2 million unique visitors and 11.7 million plays. One person could play many songs.    2018–20 · Competing for scale  A $115 million funding round backed expansion. Spotify launched in India in 2019. By 2020 Gaana reported 185 million monthly active users.    2022 · A different price of entry  Gaana ended free streaming and asked listeners to subscribe. A casual listener could keep using rival free services without making that decision. Mirchi separately launched Mirchi Plus for original shows.    2023–26 · Rebuilding paid listening  ENIL acquired the Gaana undertaking in December 2023. By the September 2026 quarter, management was discussing the cost of attracting paying users and the timing of breakeven.    Read the contemporary evidence.  Early web usage  ·  Funding and reported reach  ·  2022 paid pivot  ·  ENIL FY25 annual report  ·  ENIL earnings call, November 2026  "},{"title":"Gaana & digital · Why did Spotify gain while Gaana fell?","url":"/radio-mirchi/digital#listener-choice","text":"  Share of urban Indian respondents using each service    Service  2021  2024  Change      Gaana     32%     22%  -10 points    Spotify     24%     42%  +18 points    JioSaavn     30%     24%  -6 points    YouTube     66%     53%  -13 points     Spotify moved ahead of Gaana in this survey. Respondents could use several services. The survey cannot tell us whether a particular listener switched apps or why. YouTube here is the survey’s YouTube category.  YouGov India Media Morph, 2024    What made Spotify easier to choose?  Free listening reduced the risk of trying it. Spotify also invested in local discovery. It reported that international music accounted for nearly 70% of listening at launch in India, while local music exceeded 70% five years later. A listener who found familiar music, built playlists and kept returning had a reason to stay. The paywall change and local discovery are plausible explanations. Neither explains a measured fraction of Gaana’s decline.  Spotify India at five years     What does the 300 million headline tell us?  Spotify reached 300 million paying subscribe"},{"title":"Gaana & digital · What can an advertiser buy from Mirchi?","url":"/radio-mirchi/digital#brand-partnerships","text":" A brand can pay for access to an audience, for a creative team to make something, or for an event that people attend. A contract may combine all three. Count its revenue once.   M-Ping · buy targeted advertising  A local retailer can specify the audience and pay to deliver a recorded message across participating publishers. Software selects eligible placements. Ads may run before or during audio. A companion banner gives a listener something to tap where supported. Confirm targeting, publisher access and dynamic insertion in the current order. Measure completed listens, cost per thousand impressions and the cost of a qualified response.  M-Ping  ·  Mirchi launch announcement     Mirchi Brewery · commission a campaign  The creative team develops the idea and produces the work. Gradeup used Brewery for a series of brand films. A buyer might commission a host-led reel, a branded audio drama or a podcast segment. Price production, talent and distribution separately. Check completion, qualified enquiries and the money left after production costs.  ENIL FY25 annual report  ·  Gradeup camp"},{"title":"Gaana & digital · Three digital jobs, three business models","url":"/radio-mirchi/digital#portfolio","text":"   Subscription  Gaana  A consumer pays for a useful audio experience. Discovery, playback reliability, paid access and repeat listening determine value and renewal. The annual report describes a subscription-led service.   S5      Audience & content  Mirchi content  Articles, personalities, stories and social clips attract attention and can lead into deeper listening. The Mirchi web root currently leads to Reads with Gaana navigation.   S21      B2B services  Digital solutions  A brand pays for a campaign or service. The product is reliable creative and commercial delivery, not necessarily another consumer application.   S2     "},{"title":"Gaana & digital · What the public price surfaces showed","url":"/radio-mirchi/digital#pricing","text":"     Surface  Observed price / proposition  Interpretation      Gaana web trial  ₹1 / 30-day trial; says yearly auto-renew after trial.  Verify the next charge and mandate terms at checkout; no checkout completed.    Gaana web yearly  ₹709 offer; ₹799 reference price.  An observed offer, not actual Average revenue per user.    Gaana web monthly  ₹129; monthly auto-renew.  A different duration and commitment.    Gaana web one-time annual  ₹899; no auto debit.  Existing customer choice; do not propose this as absent.    Noise × Gaana  ₹1,399 hardware bundle with one year Gaana Plus.  Separate hardware price from consideration earned by Gaana.    Gaana iOS listing  SKUs include ₹119 monthly / ₹799 yearly.  Listing SKUs can differ from web and selected checkout eligibility.      Web prices from this session, bundle from the Oct announcement, iOS SKUs from the India listing. Taxes, eligibility and offer duration must be checked in the selected purchase journey.   S23   S10   S19   "},{"title":"Gaana & digital · Proposed activation and retention sequence","url":"/radio-mirchi/digital#growth","text":"     Stage  Customer value  Measurement      Intent  Preserve the artist, song, podcast or language that brought the user.  Source-linked intent to a successful content start.    Activation  Get to a satisfying listening session quickly.  Time to first successful play; paid access success.    Habit  Make returning easy through existing history, queue and discovery capabilities.  Retained listening days and successful sessions per user group.    Paid value  Explain what the selected plan gives and when it renews.  Profit after direct costs per paid user, disputes and refund requests.    Renewal  Reconnect the person with value they used; easy account control.  Profit from subscription renewals after costs and incentives.      History and queue improvements already appear in company updates. The opportunity is to validate which users benefit and whether those benefits change retention.   S4   "},{"title":"Gaana & digital · Content IP can bridge attention and payment","url":"/radio-mirchi/digital#content","text":" Sunday Suspense continues to publish: the 17 November Indrapatan announcement points audiences to Mirchi Bangla YouTube and Gaana. This is evidence of an active regional franchise, not an estimate of its commercial performance.   S14    Proposed test: preserve a listener’s chosen story or creator through a web-to-app handoff, resume them at the relevant destination and measure qualified listening and subsequent renewal. Keep a clean comparison group that does not receive the change to distinguish genuine extra activity from users who would have listened anyway.   Do not equate these metrics  Social followers, YouTube subscribers, monthly active listeners, trials, paid subscribers and billed subscribers measure different populations. Never use one as a substitute for another, and do not add platform counts into unique reach.  "},{"title":"Web, mobile & apps · What the platform evidence covers","url":"/radio-mirchi/platforms#test-depth","text":"  Tried in a browser:  Mirchi discovery and the handoff to Gaana, regional series pages and a brief web playback start. Mobile web was checked at a simulated phone width.   Checked in app stores:  listings, descriptions and release notes. Installed-app login, playback after a call, offline listening and purchases still need a device test. Public storefront evidence cannot establish whether these tasks succeed.  The new evidence confirms the integration of Mirchi Plus into Gaana and identifies the publicly visible episode and subscription links. A signed-in test is still needed to verify whether an existing Mirchi account preserves its library, subscription and session.  Follow the observed journey  "},{"title":"Web, mobile & apps · Platform coverage and depth","url":"/radio-mirchi/platforms#coverage","text":"     Surface  What was checked  Depth / outcome      Mirchi desktop web  Root, Reads, navigation, subscription handoff, mobile-app landing.  Live browser at default 1280 × 720. Root leads to /stories; Gaana links and app QR visible.   S21   S20      Mirchi mobile web  Reads and app handoff at 390 × 844.  Responsive browser emulation; document width 390px. No physical handset used.   S21      Gaana desktop web  Home, plan page, radio, podcast listing, series detail and app-store links.  Live public journey. Subscription options and sign-in controls inspected; no payment.   S22   S23   S24   S25      Gaana mobile web  Public discovery and navigation at 390 × 844.  Responsive controls observed. Radio document measured 728px wide at 390px viewport; reproduce and isolate overflow before grading severity.   S24      Mirchi Android  Listing, metadata, update date, rating and description.  Live listing inspected. Installed app, OTP, playback and offline mode not tested.   S16      Mirchi iOS  Website handoff and India / Qatar storefront availability.  India URL showed page not found; Qatar l"},{"title":"Web, mobile & apps · Observed findings, without overstating impact","url":"/radio-mirchi/platforms#observations","text":"   Observed / needs validation  O1 · Mirchi-to-Gaana transition  Mirchi Reads uses Gaana navigation and subscription calls to action; the separate app landing still promotes Mirchi Plus. That is an observed mixed destination story, not proof users are confused.   S21   S20     Validate:  can a new user explain which app they need and preserve their intended content through the handoff?  Measure:  destination success and retained listening.    Observed / scoped  O2 · Mobile accessibility constraint  Mirchi Reads declares a viewport with user-scalable=no. At 390px, the first article heading appeared around 522px from the top in this session, following navigation and an ad region.   S21     Validate:  pinch / browser zoom and first-content visibility on real devices with and without ads.  Test:  allow zoom and reduce non-content space while monitoring ad profit after direct costs.    Observed / region-specific  O3 · App availability needs a regional check  The India Mirchi iOS URL returned page not found; the app-download landing links a US storefront, while Qatar metadata remains acces"},{"title":"Web, mobile & apps · App evidence: current release versus legacy storefront","url":"/radio-mirchi/platforms#apps","text":"     App / surface  Snapshot  What it does and does not establish      Mirchi Plus Android  Live browser: 2.9 stars, ~1.82K reviews, 1M+ downloads; update 30 Mar 2024.   S16    A legacy public listing remains. Search cache differed; rating is not a full user-sentiment study.    Mirchi Plus iOS Qatar  Version 7.5, 1 Apr 2024.   S17    Regional metadata only. India availability could not be established.    Gaana Android  4.2 stars, 100M+ downloads; retrieved update 4 Nov 2026.   S18    Active release metadata and large lifetime distribution. Downloads do not equal active or paying listeners.    Gaana iOS India  4.1 stars, ~114K ratings; version 9.26.4 shown two days ago.   S19    Current release evidence, supported devices and store SKUs. Not installed-app QA.       Reviews: avoid a false finding  The public pages surfaced old featured reviews as well as current metadata. I did not scrape a recent, deduplicated representative sample, so I do not claim that historical billing, ads or playback complaints describe the current release.  "},{"title":"Web, mobile & apps · Cross-platform test cases to complete with devices and accounts","url":"/radio-mirchi/platforms#journeys","text":"     Journey  Required checks  Business reason      Acquire / restore  Web, Android, iOS; phone / email identity; existing subscriber restore; partner redemption; source intent.  Prevent paid or partner users from losing access.    Listen  First play, queue, search, language, resume, background, Bluetooth, lock screen, interruption and weak network.  Prove the listening habit works in the actual context.    Offline / devices  Download, airplane mode, expiry, device switch; Watch / TV / car where supported.  Verify the paid promise and device-specific continuity.    Billing control  Full renewal disclosure, mandate, receipt, cancellation, restore and support escalation.  Protect trust and reliable recurring revenue.    Attend / return  Social / radio source, event detail, booking platform, total price, ticket retrieval, entry and post-event communication.  Connect conversion to a useful experience and a return relationship.    Participate  Current eligibility, optional permissions, photo flow, voting rules, error states and consent records.  Make campaign participation clear and opera"},{"title":"Current initiatives · Which digital features had already shipped?","url":"/radio-mirchi/initiatives#release-history","text":" Use the date ENIL reported each feature when discussing a new idea. A launch establishes that a feature existed. Current eligibility, regional availability and commercial impact need their own evidence.   Before the acquisition · online stations already used Gaana  Mirchi Activation featured in the March 2006 deck. By FY10 Mirchi was distributing audio on Airtel, followed by other operators. Mirchi Top 20 extended into television in FY14. Mirchi Play was reported in FY18. By FY20 there were 24 Mirchi Play online stations operating on Gaana. FY21 reported 25 on Gaana’s landing page, including Mirchi Campus. ENIL acquired the Gaana undertaking in December 2023, years after the initial distribution relationship.  Investor archive  ·  FY21 filing     FY25–26 · reduce the effort of changing apps and finding music  Gaana reported a new Android and iOS version and an affiliate subscription campaign. Later decks describe importing playlists, an automatically refreshed offline mix, local trending tracks and Dolby Atmos support. Collaborative playlists let friends edit together. Regional char"},{"title":"Current initiatives · When did the main products and campaigns appear?","url":"/radio-mirchi/initiatives#timeline","text":"     Period  What happened  Why it matters      FY23  Mirchi Plus was already operating. ENIL discussed its digital audience in its May 2023 results.  This establishes that the platform existed by then.    FY24  ENIL acquired the Gaana business and began integrating Mirchi Plus with it.  An acquisition brought an existing music service into ENIL.    FY25  Mirchi Brewery reported MG Hector showroom drives and a Dulux dealer display contest.  ENIL FY25 annual report, pp. 15–16   Client campaigns delivered during the year. First launch dates were not disclosed.    FY26  ENIL reported work on listening history and lyrics search, alongside events including the Mindspace Eco Run.   S4    Product updates and event editions have different measures of success.    FY27 through September 2026  ENIL reported Gaana distribution through Vivo and Samsung TV, and the Mirchi Par AI-GIRI campaign.   S1    Check whether each distribution deal brings listeners back and whether each campaign delivers for sponsors.      This timeline covers documented milestones. Dates are reporting periods unless an exac"},{"title":"Current initiatives · Current and recent initiative register","url":"/radio-mirchi/initiatives#register","text":" Filter initiatives   All initiatives  Gaana product & distribution  Mirchi & local campaigns  Events & participation       Launched, Oct 2026  Noise bundle  One-year premium bundle.   S10     Question to build on it  How many eligible purchasers redeem, activate, retain and later renew?     Reported Q2 FY27  Samsung TV + Vivo distribution  TV availability; phone pre-installation.   S1     Question to build on it  Do device user groups produce extra, profitable listening after cost of getting a new customer?     Reported Q2 FY27  Queue & mood controls  Contextual queue updates.   S1     Question to build on it  Which contexts improve successful listening and paid retention?     Reported Q2 FY27  UMG early access  Selected releases 72 hours early.   S1     Question to build on it  Does exclusivity change paid conversion or just shift listening time?     Reported Q2 FY27  DISCVR / Off The Record / Unplugged  Artist-led formats.   S1     Question to build on it  Which formats create retained listeners after production cost?     Reported Q4 FY26  Web 2.0 / listening history / lyrics sear"},{"title":"Current initiatives · Implications for future investment","url":"/radio-mirchi/initiatives#respect","text":" Confirm the owner, release date and uptake of existing products before commissioning another version. City teams can assess local participation and sponsor delivery. Subscription plans and device distribution require the Gaana team. "},{"title":"AI today & next · Where ENIL documents AI in a real product","url":"/radio-mirchi/ai#deployed-audio","text":" Gaana’s Q1 FY27 deck describes personalised mixes and recommendation widgets for premium listeners on desktop and mobile web. It also describes listening history and a queue that can continue playback. Q2 attributes higher plays per subscriber to improvements in how songs are matched. ENIL reports the engagement signal without publishing a controlled estimate of the revenue gained.  Q1 FY27 presentation  ·  ENIL Q2 FY27 presentation   Mirchi Delhi’s AI-Giri campaign used AI-produced station identifiers and interviews with specialists. ENIL reported cumulative Instagram reach above 500,000. This is a documented production use and a campaign audience measure.  ENIL Q2 FY27 presentation  "},{"title":"AI today & next · Documented use in India","url":"/radio-mirchi/ai#india","text":" For Muthoot Finance’s Maha Kumbh campaign, Mirchi Brewery described using AI to make short films about devotees. The report also describes the locker service and registrations. It gives no separate sales result or production savings from the films.  ENIL FY25 annual report, pp. 15–16   For a station pilot, a producer could use AI to suggest clips from a cleared recording, then measure editing time per approved clip. This proposal needs editorial approval. The UAE presenter, device features and Gaana recommendations below have different owners. "},{"title":"AI today & next · Summary of documented uses","url":"/radio-mirchi/ai#summary","text":" “Mirchi has already experimented with AI presenters, station branding, campaigns, images and event photo delivery. Gaana also reports new voice controls through Apple. I would build on this work with tools that help teams prepare and reuse content, serve advertisers and help listeners find the right music or story. I would start with one workflow, measure the time and money it saves, and expand after the team finds the output useful.”  Existing examples are documented below. Every proposed use is a suggestion for validation. The public record cannot reveal every internal tool, supplier or experiment. "},{"title":"AI today & next · What is already documented","url":"/radio-mirchi/ai#existing","text":"     Area  What the source establishes  Status and date  Question to ask      AI radio presenter  Airah in Mirchi UAE, with AI-driven presenting, content and social posts.   S39    Historical FY23 disclosure.  Is it still running, and what did it change in production cost, audience response and advertiser demand?    Station audio and AI education  AI-produced station IDs and expert conversations in Delhi’s AI-Giri campaign. Company reported 500K+ Instagram reach.   S1    Reported Q2 FY27.  How much was a one-off campaign, and what became a regular production tool?    Voice control for streaming  Mirchi reports Gaana actions through Siri and Apple Intelligence, plus Spotlight discovery.   S40    Reported September 2026. Native test pending.  Which devices, languages and actions work reliably? Does voice use lead to more successful listening?    Event photography  AI-powered real-time runner photo delivery at Mindspace Eco Run.   S4    Reported Q4 FY26.  How are participants matched to photos, what permission is obtained and how accurate and fast is delivery?    Visual production  An a"},{"title":"AI today & next · Where I would start","url":"/radio-mirchi/ai#priority","text":"     Order  First use  Why it is worth testing  Decision measure      1  Turn a recorded show into a searchable transcript, suggested clips and draft captions.  One recording can support several existing channels. Editors can judge usefulness quickly.  Minutes of staff work per approved clip, cost per approved asset, factual errors and return listening.    2  Help sales teams prepare a campaign proposal and delivery report.  Uses existing offers, rate cards and campaign records. Reduces time spent assembling information.  Time per approved proposal, win rate, delivery errors and profit after serving the client.    3  Help listeners describe the music or story they want in everyday language.  Builds on Gaana search and recommendation work. Start with one language and a small catalogue.  Successful listening starts, search abandonment, skips and return after 7 and 30 days.    4  Help event teams forecast ticket demand and check costs.  Supports decisions before large vendor commitments. Needs clean historical data.  Forecast error, event profit, unsold capacity and cash exposed before "},{"title":"AI today & next · Operations, advertising and event opportunities","url":"/radio-mirchi/ai#operations","text":"  Explore proposed uses and measures      Team / task  Proposed assistance  How it helps  What people still approve      RJ preparation  Search approved local stories, previous shows and guest notes. Draft a short briefing with links.  Less preparation time and easier access to the archive.  Facts, local relevance, script and on-air delivery.    Production  Suggest time-coded clips, captions, titles and language-specific versions.  More approved output from the same recording.  Context, humour, accuracy, talent permission and final edit.    Ad delivery  Compare broadcast logs and approved scripts with booked spots. Flag missing or mismatched delivery.  Fewer missed commitments and faster campaign reporting.  Whether an exception needs a replacement spot or client remedy.    Sales  Draft a proposal from the client’s objective using approved packages and availability.  Faster turnaround and more consistent offers.  Price, promised results, inventory and contract.    Client reporting  Assemble delivery evidence, costs and results into a draft report.  Less manual reporting and clearer r"},{"title":"AI today & next · Streaming and podcast opportunities","url":"/radio-mirchi/ai#streaming","text":"  Explore proposed uses and measures      Customer need  Proposed experience  Business measure  Quality check      “I know the mood, but not a song.”  Describe language, activity and mood, then preview a short playlist built from the licensed catalogue.  First successful play, skips, listening days and renewal.  Every suggested track must exist and be available to that listener.    “I heard a line, but forgot the title.”  Improve mixed-language and imperfect-lyric search, building on existing lyrics search.   S4    Search success and time to play.  Test real misspellings and regional pronunciation with consented samples.    “Help me continue my story.”  Use the saved listening position and an editor-approved recap before resuming.  Episode completion and return to the series.  Keep spoilers out and let the listener skip the recap.    “Find a story like the one I loved.”  Recommend by language, theme, pace and available time using reviewed episode descriptions.  Starts that become meaningful listening, then return visits.  Test whether recommendations are varied and relevant.    “I wa"},{"title":"AI today & next · New products and commercial ideas to validate","url":"/radio-mirchi/ai#launches","text":"  Explore proposed uses and measures      Idea  Who it serves and what they receive  Possible way to earn  Small first test      Mirchi Creator Desk  RJs and podcast teams upload a recording and receive editable clips, chapters, captions and show notes.  Internal time savings first. A paid creator service could follow if external demand is established.  Use one show and one editor. Compare total production time and approved output with the current process.    Gaana Listen My Way  Listeners describe a situation in everyday language and receive a playable selection.  Improved subscription use and renewal. Test paid demand only after proving the listening benefit.  One language, one device and the existing catalogue. Compare with current search and playlists.    Mirchi Local Brand Studio  A local business gives its city, offer and budget. The sales team receives an editable radio and social campaign draft.  Campaign fee, repeat advertiser spend and optional production charges.  One advertiser category in two cities, with approved offers and human sales review.    Mirchi Story Explorer  "},{"title":"AI today & next · How to judge the money and time saved","url":"/radio-mirchi/ai#value","text":"  For staff tools, count the complete task. Include checking and correcting AI output. Saving drafting time helps only when total time per approved result falls.  For streaming, compare similar groups receiving the new and existing experience. Track successful plays, return after 7 and 30 days, subscription renewal and profit after content, payment, support and AI costs.  For advertising, track approved proposal time, win rate, price achieved, delivery, collections and repeat spend. Include whether a new package takes money away from an existing package.  For events, measure demand forecast error, ticket income, refunds, sponsor renewal and actual profit after direct costs. Count vendor commitments made before cash is collected.  For a new paid AI product, test whether customers pay and return. Include model usage, audio processing, storage, editing, support and sales costs.    Illustrative calculation.  If 20 editors each save 30 minutes a day over 22 working days, that is 220 hours per month. At an assumed ₹500 per hour, the capacity value is ₹1.10 lakh. After an assumed ₹30,000 mo"},{"title":"AI today & next · The first 90 days for AI","url":"/radio-mirchi/ai#delivery","text":"     Period  Work  Evidence needed to continue      Days 1-15  Map tools already used by each team. Observe real tasks. Record time, errors, cost and who approves the result.  One repeated task with a clear owner and enough examples to evaluate.    Days 16-30  Build the content assistant or proposal assistant around approved source material. Compare it with a template and the current workflow.  Useful output after review, with acceptable cost and fewer total staff minutes.    Days 31-60  Run a limited team pilot. Track corrections, rejected outputs and time per completed task.  The team keeps using it and the whole task becomes cheaper or faster without a quality decline.    Days 61-90  Expand the successful workflow. Test a small listener-facing idea if the data, rights and team are ready.  Measured customer benefit, an owner for ongoing support and a clear spending limit.      A transcript-and-clip assistant is my provisional first choice because the team can review its output and measure its value quickly. A large new voice or music product needs stronger proof of demand and right"},{"title":"AI today & next · Questions I would ask the Mirchi team","url":"/radio-mirchi/ai#questions","text":"  Which AI tools already save staff time, and how is that measured?  Is Airah still in use, and what did the experiment teach the team?  Which Gaana discovery and voice features use AI, and what improved in controlled tests?  How much does it cost to produce and repurpose one approved episode or campaign today?  What permissions cover talent voices, stories, music, transcripts and new language versions?  Who owns the AI budget, output quality and ongoing support?  Which customer or business result should the first AI pilot improve?  "},{"title":"Sources & research limits · Investor presentations and Stories coverage","url":"/radio-mirchi/sources#presentation-archive","text":" Review dated 23 November 2026. ENIL lists 22 fiscal years. Its rendered archive contains 108 PDF links pointing to 107 distinct URLs, including call transcripts. The FY21 Q4 link was recovered from the exchange filing. The FY09 Q2 presentation link returned an error page, so that entry links to the quarterly results as supporting evidence. Some archive captions repeat or refer to a different quarter. Prefer the date inside the linked document.  The current Stories landing page supplied 30 linked editorial and photo features. Across 58 publicly listed sitemap files, the review indexed 20,475 distinct URLs and retrieved 253 brand- or product-matched article and photo-story pages. The sitemap includes unrelated entertainment coverage and older pages. This is a title-based screen of the wider archive and a full-page review of the selected material.  Live Stories page  ·  Publisher sitemap    FY2027 · 4 documents listed    Earnings call transcript Q2FY27    Investors Presentation Q2FY27    Earnings call transcript Q1FY27    Investors Presentation Q1FY27      FY2026 · 8 documents listed  "},{"title":"Sources & research limits · What the additional reading contributes","url":"/radio-mirchi/sources#digital-reading","text":" The  ENIL media archive  documents the earlier FM expansion.  Fortune India  describes changing access to FM receivers and advertiser demand for measurable outcomes. Both help explain why a broadcaster would invest in digital distribution.   Business Today on Gen Z  supports testing whether younger buyers understand the value and trust an offer. Willingness to pay for a Mirchi show still requires a listening and pricing experiment. The  competitive comparison  links the survey, India price check and Spotify disclosures. The shared LinkedIn commentary was unavailable. Mirchi’s published Product Manager role covers consumer web and mobile, roadmap ownership, experiments, engagement and monetisation. "},{"title":"Sources & research limits · Research method and confidence","url":"/radio-mirchi/sources#method","text":" Research date:  21 November 2026, India time . Financial cut-off: latest available Q2 / H1 FY27 disclosures. Source hierarchy: filed financial tables for scoped figures; management disclosures for strategy; official product pages for current propositions; public observations for experience; independent industry research for market context.      Label  Meaning  Limit      Reported  Company / official source says it.  Not independently audited unless explicitly stated.    Observed  A public browser surface was inspected in this session.  Session, region, viewport and eligibility may affect behaviour.    Listing evidence  Store description, release notes, ratings or screenshots.  Does not establish installed-app behaviour.    Hypothesis / proposed  Original analysis or a potential test.  Not a confirmed defect or promised business result.      Public browsing used a signed-out in-app browser. Desktop default was 1280 × 720. Mobile responsive checks used a 390 × 844 viewport; these are browser emulation, not a physical handset or native app test. No subscription or ticket purchase was c"},{"title":"Sources & research limits · Reconciliation and evidence cautions","url":"/radio-mirchi/sources#cautions","text":"  Q2 EBITDA: domestic ₹11.26 crore / +9.5%; consolidated ₹12.05 crore / +5.9%. Different scopes explain different headlines.  March cash: consolidated approximately ₹423.9 crore, standalone ₹404.2 crore, distinguished in Q4 deck.  The Q2 deck executive summary prints digital revenue as ₹33 million, inconsistent with its 29% share. The press release gives ₹33 crore; the domestic minus existing business bridge is approximately ₹32.93 crore. Use that cross-check.  Annual narrative mix percentages and “digital as % of core radio” use different or unclear denominators. They are not combined into a precise annual pie chart.  The company profile’s 38M listener claim uses IRS 2019. Latest deck reach / event-count claims vary across slides; do not add them or invent a unique audience count.  Mirchi Plus store cache and live ratings differ. The live observed rating is recorded with its date rather than presented as a universal value.  Featured reviews include 2019-2023 and earlier years. They are not used to claim current defect prevalence or recent sentiment.  Mirchi iOS India URL was unavail"},{"title":"Sources & research limits · Source register","url":"/radio-mirchi/sources#registry","text":" Find a source       S1 · 3-4 Nov 2026   ENIL Q2 FY27 investor presentation   Financial tables: PDF pp. 15-17. Initiatives: pp. 19-31. Company presentation; audience claims are not independently audited.  https://www.enil.co.in/pdf/stock_exchange_fillings/FY27/ENILInvestorsPresentationQ2FY27.pdf    S2 · 3 Nov 2026   ENIL Q2 FY27 results press release   Quarter ended 30 Sep 2026. Rounded revenue, domestic mix, digital losses and consolidated cash.  https://www.enil.co.in/pdf/stock_exchange_fillings/FY27/ENILPressReleaseQ2FY27.pdf    S3 · 4 Nov; filed 6 Nov 2026   ENIL Q2 FY27 earnings call transcript   Management commentary, not a forecast: radio pressure, event margin discipline, acquisition costs and Gaana ambition.  https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/ENIL_06112026152711_ENIL20261106TranscriptQ2FY27.pdf    S4 · 18 May 2026   ENIL Q4 FY26 investor presentation   FY26 consolidated table: PDF p. 19. Product updates pp. 21-25; event cases pp. 26-29.  https://www.enil.co.in/pdf/stock_exchange_fillings/FY26/2026_05_18_Investor_PPT_Q4FY26.pdf    S5 · FY ended 31 Mar 2026   ENIL FY2"},{"title":"Gaana & digital · Pricing: reconcile the actual bill, duration and renewal","url":"/radio-mirchi/digital#pricing-trust","text":"Pricing: reconcile the actual bill, duration and renewal Reported displayed math: ₹709 “yearly” is shown as ₹58.27/month; ₹709 ÷ 12 is ₹59.08 and ₹709 ÷ 13 is ₹54.54 (rounded). ₹58.27 × 12 = ₹699.24. The ₹1,399 Noise Buds R1 bundle is displayed as ₹114.99/month but ₹1,399 ÷ 12 is ₹116.58 . These are display discrepancies based on the reported numbers : investigate whether the UI is dividing a different qualifying price or term before attributing a billing error. Never treat bundled hardware consideration as pure music ARPU. Visible price Verified / observed meaning Required disclosure ₹709/year Promotional annual amount, reported charged upfront on iOS. Bill today, 12 versus 13 months, eligibility, renewal date and amount. ₹799 Crossed-out yearly reference shown with ₹709; a separately selectable ₹799 tier is not established . Only advertise a like-for-like real reference price. ₹899/year Gaana web separately listed a one-time annual option without auto-debit; iOS SKU parity still needs testing. Pay once versus auto-renew, actual duration and included benefits. ₹1,399 bundle Noise Buds R1 with music access; a hardware + digital offer. Hardware, delivery, included music entitlement, any later renewal and cancellation. ₹129/month Observed monthly subscription option, with a potentially obstructed CTA. Monthly billing, renewals and identical entitlement labels across surfaces. Recommended hierarchy: “Annual, auto-renewing”, “Annual, pay once” and “Headphones + music” only if actual live SKUs support each choice. Show a single feature matrix across Upgrade, popup and checkout (ad-free listening, audio quality, offline, Party Mode, bundle). Never invent a “standard” and “premium” tier to rationalise the three prices."},{"title":"Market & competitors · What should be difficult to copy?","url":"/radio-mirchi/competition#relationship-position","text":"What should be difficult to copy? YouTube Music benefits from YouTube's creator/remix and video ecosystem and some bundles; Spotify has broad discovery and continuity. Exact India catalogue, plan and feature comparisons must be checked by market and date. Gaana cannot assume catalogue or pricing parity. A generic AI DJ is easy for competitors to build. A permissioned network of recognisable Mirchi RJs, regional editorial judgment, local rituals and social dedications could create cultural intimacy: it becomes a defensible advantage only if users return more often and the full cost of that relationship is sustainable. Falsification test: randomise eligible listeners between a rights-cleared RJ ritual and a comparable non-RJ curated experience. Evaluate two-day weekly listening, D7/D30, opt-outs and retained contribution after royalties, speech inference and content costs. Abandon the moat claim if lift is absent. Full proposition ."},{"title":"Business case · Executive verdict","url":"/radio-mirchi#executive-verdict","text":"Executive verdict · 23 Nov 2026 Priority 1: make playback and purchase trustworthy before increasing paid promotion. Supplied Gaana iOS captures show competing first-scroll promotions, ambiguous yearly prices, inconsistent benefits and obscured actions. The repeated locked-close modal is reported and requires device reproduction. Priority 2: test whether regional Mirchi voices, Indian rituals and dedications generate meaningful repeat listening and contribution that Spotify/YouTube-style feature copying cannot cheaply replace. Evidence · Thesis · Gated plan ."},{"title":"Business case · The decision facing Mirchi Digital","url":"/radio-mirchi#brief","text":"The decision facing Mirchi Digital The recommendation in one sentence Make the app easy and trustworthy first. Then test whether familiar Mirchi voices and Indian music moments give people a reason to listen again. See the steps . When a listener hears a Mirchi host on FM or sees a clip online, can Mirchi help them find the full show, return next week and eventually pay for more? Start with one city and one recurring show. Mirchi supplies the host, programme and promotion. A Gaana product partner would own changes to its player, plans and billing. In July–September 2026 ENIL reported ₹33 crore in digital revenue, up 4.6% year on year and equal to 29% of domestic revenue. Digital still recorded an EBITDA loss of ₹7.5 crore, compared with ₹9.8 crore a year earlier. EBITDA measures earnings before interest, taxes, depreciation and amortisation. Management flagged a possible one- to two-quarter delay to Gaana’s breakeven aim because bringing in customers cost more. ENIL earnings call, November 2026 Follow a reader from Mirchi Stories into Gaana · See ticketed and sponsor-funded events · Browse the investor archive by year"},{"title":"First 90 days · From a frustrating first visit to a listening habit","url":"/radio-mirchi/plan#gaana-90","text":"From a frustrating first visit to a listening habit THE PRIORITY · GAANA MUSIC APP The supplied Gaana iPhone screens show paid-plan buttons being covered by the music player, crowded subscription promotions and confusing prices. A frequently reopening subscription popup was also reported. Those are reasons to investigate and fix the experience before spending effort on new AI features. Seen in the screenshots Covered buttons and confusing offers Reported by the tester Repeated subscription popup Not yet established How many users leave or stop paying THE IDEA IN ONE GLANCE 1 Make listening easy Remove interruptions and fix what is broken. 2 Make returning rewarding Try familiar voices and Indian listening moments. 3 Earn the subscription Ask when a useful premium benefit is needed. What happens over the 90 days? The dates below are an example sequence, not promises. The next stage starts only if the previous work is safe, usable and supported by evidence. 01 Days 1–15 Understand the problem See exactly where people struggle Watch new and returning listeners try to play music, close offers and choose a plan. Check the actual prices shown at payment. Example Does the ₹709 plan charge immediately? Why is the monthly figure different when we divide it by 12? Before moving on: we can reproduce the problems, show screenshots of each issue and explain the real payment terms. 02 Days 16–30 Fix the basics Let the listener stay in control Stop subscription offers appearing again and again, make Close work immediately, move the music player away from purchase buttons and make plan differences readable. Example When someone taps a monthly plan, they can read its price and tap Subscribe without the floating player blocking it. Before moving on: key buttons work, payment information "},{"title":"First 90 days · What about Radio Mirchi's stations and advertisers?","url":"/radio-mirchi/plan#sequence","text":"What about Radio Mirchi's stations and advertisers? A SEPARATE BUSINESS PROBLEM Not every improvement belongs to Gaana. Mirchi also needs better ways to help local advertisers get value from campaigns and decide which events are worth repeating. This is a separate workstream , not four more things for one Gaana team to build. 01 First month: understand a station Talk to listeners, producers and advertisers in one city. Find the most important repeated problem. 02 Second month: fix one issue Try one improvement, such as easier campaign reporting or finding a popular show online. 03 Third month: check real results Did advertisers book again? Did the change save time or make more money after its costs? Show the detailed station delivery checklist Days 1–15: confirm ownership and measurement. Days 16–30: agree the problem, cost and an honest comparison. Days 31–60: release one focused improvement with tracking. Days 61–90: review customer results, cash collected and direct costs, then decide whether to repeat it in another city. One city and one accountable owner come before expansion. Read the business recommendations ."},{"title":"First 90 days · Who would actually do this?","url":"/radio-mirchi/plan#stakeholders","text":"Who would actually do this? Mirchi and Gaana are different operating teams. This is the proposed responsibility split; it does not assume approval or access to internal systems. Gaana team Own the app changes Player layout, subscription screens, payment terms, experiments and reliable listening. Mirchi team Supply the human connection Host participation, regional stories, local programming and creator relationships. Finance, legal and data Check it is safe and worth doing Voice and music permission, cost, listener privacy and fair measurement."},{"title":"First 90 days · How would decisions get made?","url":"/radio-mirchi/plan#cadence","text":"How would decisions get made? Each week, review what listeners are struggling with. Every two weeks, check whether the changes worked for real people. At the end of each month, decide what deserves more time and money. A promising idea is not enough if the experience gets worse or its costs exceed its value. Keep going if people benefit Improve if the signal is mixed Stop if harm or cost outweighs value"},{"title":"First 90 days · Three things I would confirm in the interview","url":"/radio-mirchi/plan#questions","text":"Three things I would confirm in the interview Which of these businesses would I actually own: station products, Gaana, or both? Which product changes and customer data would I have permission to work with? What real outcome would count as a successful first 90 days for the hiring team? Show additional planning considerations Before promising a roadmap, also agree the available engineering and editorial capacity, existing in-flight work, finance definitions, which cities matter most, and who has final authority over pricing and app releases."},{"title":"Web, mobile & apps · People came to play music. The app keeps selling to them.","url":"/radio-mirchi/platforms#gaana-ios-audit","text":"People came to play music. The app keeps selling to them. GAANA IPHONE APP · WHAT WAS OBSERVED The supplied iPhone screenshots show a music player covering important buttons, paid offers competing with playlists, and pricing that is difficult to interpret. A repeating subscription popup was also reported. The first job is to make listening and buying understandable. Visible in supplied screenshots Covered buttons, multiple offers, conflicting messages Reported by the user Recurring popup with delayed Close button Still needs testing How often it happens and how many customers it affects WHY THE BOTTOM NAVIGATION NEEDS TO BE FIXED · SIMPLIFIED ILLUSTRATION, NOT AN ACTUAL APP SCREENSHOT Currently observed Monthly plan · ₹129 Subscribe now ♫ Now playing ▷ Home &nbsp; Search &nbsp; Upgrade The player and floating navigation cover the action the user came to tap. What good looks like Monthly plan · ₹129 Subscribe now ♫ Now playing ▷ Home &nbsp; Search &nbsp; Upgrade Buttons and song rows stay above the player, with enough room to scroll and tap. What I would fix, in order P0 means fix the essentials first, P1 means improve the experience next, and P2 means polish the details. These labels describe priority, not proven revenue impact. P0 · FIX FIRST · LISTENING CONTROL Stop forcing people back into the subscription screen The issue: the tester reports a full-screen offer returning every 1–2 minutes, with Close temporarily locked. The fix: let Close work immediately, remember dismissal and offer paid plans only when someone requests a benefit. How I would confirm the change Reproduce across iOS account states, then count interrupted sessions, offer dismissals, successful first plays, complaints and later return. Churn or App Store review impact is not proven by the screenshots"},{"title":"Gaana & digital · Why would someone choose Gaana again tomorrow?","url":"/radio-mirchi/digital#india-own-app","text":"Why would someone choose Gaana again tomorrow? THE PRODUCT IDEA · GAANA A music app cannot rely only on having songs or offering a discount. YouTube Music and Spotify already give many people easy access to music. My idea is to make Gaana feel more personal to everyday life in India using Mirchi's familiar voices, languages, rituals and communities. This is a proposal to test, not a claim that Gaana has proved these features work. Start by fixing the listening and paywall problems seen in the iPhone audit. The competition people already know Find almost any song. Discover popular artists. Listen on familiar devices. → A reason Gaana could feel different “This is my RJ, my language, my commute, my memories and my people.” Five ideas, each built around a real listening moment ♫ 01 · YOUR FAMILIAR VOICE An RJ who understands your day Imagine: A short Hinglish or regional voice intro before a song during your commute. You can always mute or skip it. How I would test it Start with one host and approved voice rights, verified trivia and an optional 10-second introduction. Check whether people return more often than with a normal playlist, after counting voice-generation and rights costs. Location, mood and weather must be optional and appropriately sourced. ☀ 02 · YOUR DAILY RITUAL The right music for the moment Imagine: Morning bhakti, chai-time 90s, Friday Punjabi or songs for a haldi. You choose the moments that matter. How I would test it Offer opt-in, time-aware listening in one region first. See whether listeners return for that same moment, with no aggressive notifications or unwanted assumptions about them. ♡ 03 · YOUR PEOPLE Listen together, dedicate a song Imagine: Invite friends to a small “Mehfil” music room on WhatsApp and attach a 15-second spoken dedication. Ho"},{"title":"What I would improve · Don't build five features while the basics are broken","url":"/radio-mirchi/opportunities#gaana-pilots","text":"Don't build five features while the basics are broken WHAT SHOULD WE FIX FIRST? The supplied Gaana screens raise two immediate problems: parts of the app are hard to tap, and the paid offers are hard to understand. A repeated popup was also reported. Fix those basics before trying to make Gaana more personal. THE ORDER I WOULD RECOMMEND 1 Now · remove frustration Make Close work, uncover buttons and explain the plans. 2 Next · build a habit Test one familiar RJ voice and one Indian music ritual. 3 Later · grow a community Only then try dedications, fan clubs and music memories. FIRST · APP REPAIRS Help people listen without hassle Stop recurring subscription interruptions, prevent the music player from hiding buttons and show the actual amount and duration of each plan. Why first? A beautiful new feature won't help if users cannot enjoy a song or trust a payment. SECOND · SMALL USER TEST Give people a reason to return Invite a small group to try an optional Mirchi voice intro or a morning/commute playlist. Compare their voluntary return with listeners using the regular experience. Why second? Returning by choice is more valuable than opening the app after another push notification. THIRD · ONLY IF IT HELPS Try music shared with friends Test a private Mehfil song room or dedication once music rights and safety are approved. Leave fan clubs and playlist import for later validation. Why third? Sharing is useful only if friends actually listen and the experience is safe and sustainable. How would this happen? See the visual 90-day plan See what was observed Explore the five ideas Who decides? Gaana owns its app and subscription changes; Radio Mirchi contributes hosts, content and regional expertise. These are proposed experiments, not approved releases. Revenue, app quality"},{"title":"How to measure success · Did the change make listening better?","url":"/radio-mirchi/metrics#habit-metric-tree","text":"Did the change make listening better? HOW TO TELL IF IT ACTUALLY HELPED It is easy to count app downloads or subscription clicks. The more useful question is whether people can listen, choose to come back and find enough value to pay–without making the business less profitable. FOLLOW A REAL LISTENER, NOT A WALL OF NUMBERS 1 Start listening Did they successfully play what they came for? 2 Return on another day Was the music worth choosing again? 3 Use a paid benefit Did they understand the offer and decide it was worth it? THREE MEASURES I WOULD SHOW A BUSINESS HEAD ▶ First successful play Out of people trying to listen, how many actually hear the song or show? ↻ Repeat listening How many willingly listen on more than one day in a week? This would be my main proposed habit measure. ₹ Money left after costs Subscription and ad income minus the extra costs of music, AI voice, promotions and support. Always watch for hidden harm: crashes, users leaving, unwanted popups, refunds, complaints and lost ad income. No uplift or customer numbers are assumed. How I'd check the popup fix BEFORE THE CHANGE Record how often users see or dismiss the popup, whether they can start music, and whether they return a week later. AFTER THE CHANGE Allow immediate close, stop repeated timer-based interruptions and show subscription offers when someone needs a premium feature. Compare fairly: where ethical, use comparable groups and the same price/eligibility. If the old experience is harmful, fix it for everyone and be clear that a before/after comparison cannot fully prove causation. For product interviewers: detailed measures and test design Acquisition: qualified arrivals by radio, organic, paid and partner channels. Activation: successful intentional first play and time to music. Habit: we"},{"title":"Gaana and Mirchi Plus users on iOS and Android","url":"/radio-mirchi/users#four-app-userbase","text":"ENIL Gaana MAU 20M+ all digital 153.1M+ four OS profiles user base Google Play App Store downloads"},{"title":"Listening engagement, retention and cohort segmentation","url":"/radio-mirchi/users#four-app-engagement","text":"first audible play Android iOS D1 D7 D30 new returning habit paid regional Mirchi"},{"title":"28 prioritized issues across Gaana and Mirchi Plus apps","url":"/radio-mirchi/platforms#ranked-mobile-issues","text":"P0 P1 P2 paywall, blocked buttons, pricing, Android Auto, blank feed, migration, login, offline, iOS store"},{"title":"Audience implications for India-first listening","url":"/radio-mirchi/digital#mobile-audience-strategy","text":"Gaana Mirchi Plus iOS Android strategy, acquisition and culturally intimate habit"},{"title":"Four-platform engagement and commercial success scorecard","url":"/radio-mirchi/metrics#four-app-measurement","text":"audible start weekly repeat listening contribution royalties refund app active users"},{"title":"Source evidence for Gaana and Mirchi Plus audience review","url":"/radio-mirchi/sources#app-audience-evidence","text":"ENIL investor presentation Apple App Store Google Play public listing iOS Android source limitations"},{"title":"Mirchi Live product strategy: interactive online events","url":"/radio-mirchi/digital#mirchi-live","text":"Mini OTT, Mirchi Minis, original AI-assisted audio-to-video stories, comedy shows, video series, cultural songs, participatory RJ watchstreams, online-only events, India audience targeting age cohort, rights clearance, contribution metrics Mirchi Live product strategy: interactive online events"},{"title":"Priority slate for songs and mini OTT shows","url":"/radio-mirchi/opportunities#originals-priority","text":"Mini OTT, Mirchi Minis, original AI-assisted audio-to-video stories, comedy shows, video series, cultural songs, participatory RJ watchstreams, online-only events, India audience targeting age cohort, rights clearance, contribution metrics Priority slate for songs and mini OTT shows"},{"title":"90-day original IP mini-series and online watchstreams pilot","url":"/radio-mirchi/plan#originals-90","text":"Mini OTT, Mirchi Minis, original AI-assisted audio-to-video stories, comedy shows, video series, cultural songs, participatory RJ watchstreams, online-only events, India audience targeting age cohort, rights clearance, contribution metrics 90-day original IP mini-series and online watchstreams pilot"},{"title":"Original music mini OTT and online event metrics","url":"/radio-mirchi/metrics#originals-scorecard","text":"Mini OTT, Mirchi Minis, original AI-assisted audio-to-video stories, comedy shows, video series, cultural songs, participatory RJ watchstreams, online-only events, India audience targeting age cohort, rights clearance, contribution metrics Original music mini OTT and online event metrics"},{"title":"Four fully online participatory events by Mirchi","url":"/radio-mirchi/events#online-events","text":"Mini OTT, Mirchi Minis, original AI-assisted audio-to-video stories, comedy shows, video series, cultural songs, participatory RJ watchstreams, online-only events, India audience targeting age cohort, rights clearance, contribution metrics Four fully online participatory events by Mirchi"},{"title":"Current initiatives · Why reach new audiences, and which segments have evidence?","url":"/radio-mirchi/initiatives#new-audience-segments","text":"ACTUAL BUSINESS ASSETS VS NEW PRODUCT HYPOTHESES Why reach new audiences, and which segments have evidence? ENIL's Q1 FY27 investor presentation (6 August 2026) describes a multi-city, multilingual network, a large advertiser-sales organization and custom solutions. Mirchi has also documented student, community and retailer collaborations through other dated sources . These are distribution capabilities; they are not evidence that an astrology service or mental-health bot has already launched . Q1 FY27 · COMPANY REPORTED Regional and advertiser relationships ENIL describes 63 cities, 13 languages, more than 25 dialects, around 250 sales staff, 10,000+ client relationships and over 800 tailored solutions. These are organizational-scale claims, not active users of a Mirchi app. Use case: test locally relevant shows, creator communities and trackable retailer offers. FY2026 ANNUAL REPORT · SEPARATE SOURCE Retailers and neighbourhood events Mirchi reports retail partnerships, locally relevant programming and community properties, including Mirchi Back to School. This establishes precedent for merchant and educational-institution distribution, not a verified school counselling product. Use case: shop-led listening clubs, regional perks and consent-based hyperlocal programmes. 2025 CAMPAIGN · SEPARATE SOURCE Music and student wellbeing The Optum x Zoom x Radio Mirchi Happy Beats music-for-wellness collaboration reached college students with performances and wellbeing conversations. It was not presented as AI therapy or a school me"},{"title":"Gaana & digital · Keep Gaana for music. Give Mirchi its own relationship destination.","url":"/radio-mirchi/digital#mirchi-product-separation","text":"TWO PRODUCTS · TWO REASONS TO OPEN THEM Keep Gaana for music. Give Mirchi its own relationship destination. Recommendation: protect a distinct Mirchi consumer identity and experience while sharing account access, permitted content metadata, analytics definitions and deep links with Gaana. An independent Mirchi app could eventually make sense, but the first launch can be an accessible Mirchi web/app destination that proves return behaviour before paying for another native-app acquisition funnel. GAANA Play my music Fast first song, recommendations, playlists, artist discovery, offline music and clearly priced premium access. North Star: users choosing meaningful audio on multiple days Owned by: Gaana app and subscription teams Do not add: intrusive unrelated consultations and event popups MIRCHI Connect with my people Favourite RJs, original mini-series, participatory watchstreams, regional fan rooms, expert-led conversations and local communities. North Star: people voluntarily returning to a followed host, show or community Owned by: Mirchi content, platform, moderation and business partners Do not add: unlicensed consultations or misleading promises One clear connection, not one overcrowded app Shared sign-in where authorized · Consent controls · Rights-cleared deep links · Cross-surface attribution · Optional notifications Architecture choice: Mirchi web, integrated shelf or independent native app? Start: lightweight Mirchi web/PWA or retained existing Mirchi surface with a real show page, guest viewing, episode resume, o"},{"title":"Gaana & digital · Five experiences that could bring people back to Mirchi","url":"/radio-mirchi/digital#mirchi-relationship-experiences","text":"CONTENT → PARTICIPATION → TRUST → RETURN Five experiences that could bring people back to Mirchi Every proposal starts with an explicit user need and requires consent, measurable value and a safe operating model. These formats are concepts, not launched services . 01 LOWEST RISK FIRST RJ Circle: repeat conversations “I want a familiar voice and people who care about the same city, topic or music.” Scheduled RJ-hosted ask-me-anything, hobby clubs, storytelling and dedications with accessible replays and user-chosen reminders. Differentiator: real regional personalities + recurring participants, not an anonymous comment feed. Measure: opted-in attendance → meaningful contribution → next-session return. 02 LOCAL BUSINESS Mirchi Neighbourhood “I want interesting experiences near me.” Retailers and artists co-host local discovery, digital tastings, quizzes and redeemable offers. RJs add relevant editorial context without turning listeners into unsolicited marketing targets. Differentiator: regional voices + measurable local experience + a merchant sponsor. Measure: qualified attendance, opted-in enquiries, verified redemption and repeat bookings. 03 ADULTS · ENTERTAINMENT Mirchi Stars: expert-led astrology and tarot “I enjoy cultural/spiritual rituals and would like to speak to a human.” Host verified practitioners in bookable, multilingual, transparent-price 1:1 sessions or live cultural Q&As. An RJ can introduce the programme and manage community participation. Differentiator: trusted Mirchi hosts, language/cultural context, di"},{"title":"What I would improve · What to test first for Mirchi's own audience relationship","url":"/radio-mirchi/opportunities#relationship-priorities","text":"ANOTHER GROWTH ENGINE · NOT ANOTHER MUSIC FEATURE What to test first for Mirchi's own audience relationship Start with low-risk, high-frequency reasons to return. ENIL's regional RJs, retail relationships and community-event track record are usable distribution advantages. School mental-health bots and paid astrology sessions are new proposals with separate approval, safety and economics gates , not existing products. 01 · P1 PILOT RJ Circle + Mirchi Live Need: people who want a familiar regional host and a way to participate in a recurring show. MSP: RJ knows the language, city and audience story; questions or dedications genuinely shape next week's episode. Test: scheduled opt-in sessions, follow host and next-session return. 02 · P1 PILOT Retailer-led neighbourhood clubs Need: discover relevant merchants, artists and experiences locally. MSP: trusted local RJ plus usable merchant perks, measurable participation and sponsored community themes. Test: merchant trial briefs, verified opt-in actions, net contribution and sponsor renewal. 03 · GATED ADULT EXPERIMENT Mirchi Stars with real practitioners Need: culturally familiar, transparent access to spiritual and astrology conversations. MSP: vetted human pandits/tarot readers, transparent rates and choice of language, framed as personal belief/entertainment, not promised outcomes. Gate: provider checks, legal review, no financial/medical predictions, age limits, complaints and refunds. 04 · PARTNER-LED ONLY Mirchi Pause / school wellbeing Need: age-appropriate music, stress l"},{"title":"First 90 days · 90 days to prove a relationship beyond music","url":"/radio-mirchi/plan#relationship-90","text":"MIRCHI PRODUCT · INDEPENDENT TRACK 90 days to prove a relationship beyond music Gaana should remain a focused listening product. Test Mirchi's broader relationship proposition separately, using existing RJs, regional distribution and opt-in communities. None of these phases is an approved ENIL roadmap. FM / social / retail discovery → Favourite RJ or show → Voluntary participation → Meaningful return → Optional paid or sponsor value DAYS 1–15 Verify demand, assets and permissions Interview RJ followers, adults, retailers, approved education partners and qualified wellbeing professionals. Audit Mirchi Plus availability, identity, rights and actual ownership; do not treat Q1 presentation reach as app user numbers. DAYS 16–30 Create one safe Mirchi destination Build accessible host/show landing, a scheduled session, optional RSVP, safe moderation, consented events and deep links to Gaana tracks. No mandatory app installation, new accounts or upsell countdowns. DAYS 31–60 Test two practical formats Pilot an RJ Circle/watchstream and a retailer-backed community experience. Compare interactive vs replay-only format; measure voluntary return, unique responders, attrition, sponsor briefs and contribution. DAYS 61–90 Gate high-risk ideas Explore an adult-only vetted astrology/tarot expert demo only after identity, terms, legal and complaints reviews. School/college wellbeing requires educators, safeguarding and clinician oversight; do not launch an AI therapist. AFTER PILOT Choose separate native app only if it earns the cost Use rea"},{"title":"How to measure success · Is a listener becoming a returning community member?","url":"/radio-mirchi/metrics#relationship-kpis","text":"MIRCHI EXPERIENCE · A RELATIONSHIP METRIC TREE Is a listener becoming a returning community member? Proposed North Star: weekly people who voluntarily return to the same Mirchi host, community or original show and meaningfully participate. This is a product metric proposal , not ENIL's reported audience reach or Gaana MAU. Measure the separate Mirchi app/web cohort before claiming retention gains. Qualified discovery → First host/show join → Meaningful participation → 7/30-day voluntary return → Trusted commercial value Experience Value and demand metric Commercial or repeat signal Non-negotiable guardrails RJ Circle / live rooms Qualified joins, unique questions or dedications, listening/watch minutes. Next-session return, followed host, optional sponsor enquiry. Moderation, consent, user blocking, no spam or force-to-join. Retailer communities Opted-in merchant/city participation, verified useful redemptions. Qualified merchant leads, fulfilled activations, contribution and repeat bookings. Offer truth, no sensitive profiling, separation of paid placements. Vetted adult astrology/tarot Practitioner-profile comprehension, voluntarily initiated session and feedback. Transparent paid bookings, dispute-free repeat sessions, net contribution. Age gate, clear entertainment status, no fear claims, false guarantees or professional advice. Music and wellbeing Usefulness of expert-reviewed stress-literacy content and optional listening rituals. Voluntary return and appropriately used verified referral paths. No AI diagnosis, crisis "},{"title":"Sources & research limits · Regional reach, retail and student wellbeing: source-to-claim register","url":"/radio-mirchi/sources#relationship-source-check","text":"DATING AND LIMITS MATTER Regional reach, retail and student wellbeing: source-to-claim register Research reviewed 23 November 2026. ENIL's official Q1 FY27 investor PDF (6 August 2026) is linked here. The large PDF could not be opened fully by the automated document reader; public indexed text of the same presentation corroborates the company-overview figures. The source does not establish a launched Mirchi therapy chatbot, school-based AI counsellor, or paid astrology marketplace. Claims below preserve that boundary. What can be said Source and date What must not be inferred Regional reach and commercial capabilities Indexed Q1 FY27 deck , 6 August 2026: 63 cities, 13 languages, 25+ dialects, 250 sales personnel, 10,000+ client relations and 800+ custom solutions reported by ENIL. These organizational figures are not unique Mirchi app users, mental-health service adopters, live-event attendees or a qualified-lead conversion rate. Retail and educational-community precedents ENIL FY2026 annual report : retail partnerships, local programming and Mirchi Back to School among community programmes. Not proof that ENIL has contracted schools for AI counselling or operates a school mental-health service. Music and student emotional wellbeing Zoom / Optum / Radio Mirchi Happy Beats , described in 2025 coverage: college concerts, music and wellness conversations. Do not recast a college music-and-awareness activation as licensed therapy or school-age diagnosis. Possible mental-health support referral Government of India National Menta"},{"title":"Users & their needs · What ages do current listeners belong to?","url":"/radio-mirchi/users#age-audience","text":"AGE PROFILE · SOURCE-DATED, NOT GUESSED The 2026 age mix is not publicly established. ENIL publishes Gaana audience totals, but not a current age distribution or separate age profiles for Gaana iOS, Gaana Android and Mirchi Plus. The strongest brand-specific age chart I could verify is from a 2020 Gaana advertising media kit . It is useful historical context, not a current audience census. Historical Gaana audience distribution 2020 media kit · reported Google Analytics age percentages 18–24 39% 25–34 30% 35–44 21% 45–54 7% 55–64 2% 65+ 1% Historical, self-published advertising data. The displayed six groups total 100%. The 18–34 share was 69% in 2020 only. 2020 Gaana media kit . CURRENT 2026 STATUS No verified age split Do not carry the 2020 percentages forward to 2026. Company-reported Gaana MAU and lifetime Android installs have no usable age denominator. Mirchi FM's historically described 25–45 target is not a Mirchi Plus app demographic or a 2026 survey. What can be used today? Historical signal + category research + explicit age-cohort testing Meta and Ormax surveyed Indian micro-drama audiences aged 18–44 in 2025–26 and found romance, family drama and comedy prominent. Their age range is the survey population , not the age distribution of Gaana users. 2026 Meta–Ormax research . Which ages should Mirchi Originals target first? Use different content for different needs. The following groups are proposed test audiences , not claims about the current composition of Gaana or Mirchi Plus. ACQUISITION TEST 18–24 Short breaks, music discovery, sharing Proposed formats: first"},{"title":"Gaana & digital · Do not invent another audio-story product. Turn existing stories into a universe.","url":"/radio-mirchi/digital#originals-studio","text":"ORIGINAL IP · BUILD ON WHAT EXISTS Mirchi has already released original audio fiction, comedy and video shows, and its app has supported video episodes. The opportunity is new serial video IP, selective audio-to-video adaptation, original music, recognizable characters and repeatable regional franchises . Treat any existing AI-produced story masters as candidate inputs only after confirming the assets, contracts and creative quality. CURRENTLY DOCUMENTED Audio stories and entertainment assets Mirchi Plus has documented audio fiction and episodic shows. ENIL's annual reporting describes combining Mirchi Plus and Gaana. Some stories have already traveled between streaming and YouTube. This is not a proposal to launch audio stories from zero . ENIL's reported integration PROPOSED NEXT LAYER Mirchi Originals Studio + Minis Adapt rights-cleared stories to episodic vertical video. Create character-led comedy, romantic thrillers, original songs and seasonal series. Test audience response in existing channels before building a separate paid OTT app. Explore the mini-OTT concept ONE ORIGINAL STORY CAN HAVE MULTIPLE FORMATS 01 Audio master Existing licensed story, characters and voice performances 02 Video episodes 9:16 scenes with consistent faces, continuity and real editorial direction 03 Original music Theme song, character motif or standalone emotional track 04 Social discovery Scene hooks, character clips, episode recap and RJ-led promotion 05 Retained fandom Next episode, season return, live extensions and licensed adaptations Important: AI can assist production and localizati"},{"title":"Gaana & digital · Mirchi Minis","url":"/radio-mirchi/digital#mini-ott","text":"PRODUCT CONCEPT · MINI OTT WITHIN MIRCHI / GAANA Multiple original, short video series. A familiar story every time you open the app, with a reason to watch the next episode. Vertical-first Hindi + regional Audio + video 18+ audience pilots Concept preview, not a live streaming catalogue. None of the six proposed titles below is claimed to be released, licensed or playable. MIRCHI MINIS ⌕ NOW FEATURED SOCIETY NO. 420 Comedy · Episode 01 Discover Series My list START WITH AUDIENCE NEEDS, NOT A NEW APP The format is different from long-form OTT Viewers discover a short scene through a social feed, enter a clearly labelled series page, watch an actual episode, and return for the next part. A 2026 Meta–Ormax study found social feeds were the dominant way respondents discovered micro-dramas and that romance, family drama and comedy led preference. That is category research, not evidence that Gaana users have already adopted video stories . Why test 18–34 and 25–44? · Meta–Ormax 2026 research THE PROPOSED CONTENT SLATE Six series, different reasons to return Illustrative working titles and episode plans. They are not released shows, and no view, cost or conversion figures are assumed. All 6 series Comedy Romance Mystery Music Showing 6 proposed series 01 Neighbourhood comedy Society No. 420 PROPOSED SERIES 25–44 Mini series Society No. 420 A self-appointed society president bans every celebration; the tenants launch a secret festival committee. See episodes and production plan Episode plan: 90–150 sec · 12-episode test season. Reason to return: Each neighbour hides a ridiculous s"}];
